Inflation in Europe has skidded food
Accelerated inflation, measured in the eurozone, is mainly due to the rapid increase in food prices.
In November, the increase in prices, in the 13 countries of the eurozone, was greater compared to expectations, after an inflation rate of 2.6 per cent in October, an annual inflation of 3.1 per cent was recorded, said the statistics office of the European Community located in Luxembourg.
The official forecast has indicated only 3 percent, Bloomberg said.
Unlike the U.S., U.K. and Canadian central banks, the European Central Bank (ECB) has not lowered the key interest rate by saying that falling interests, along with growth in commodity prices and falling unemployment, would lead to an inflationary spiral.
The ECB would like to keep the rate of inflation below but close to two percent.
According to an analyst, it is Catch 22 for the ECB: "it is necessary to deter" inflation in order to no longer have to intervene on this subject later.
In Germany, the inflation rate of 3.3 percent is a record high over the past twelve years and in Spain it has risen from 3.6 to 4.1.
Inflation in the euro area has taken off due to the rapid rise in food and energy prices.
Cereal futures market ratings increased by 88 percent and soybean prices have also reached its highest value since 1973.
The price of food oil and dairy products also increased significantly in 2007.
This year, the global price of oil rose by 52 percent, and last month, a barrel of black gold cost almost US$100.
According to the ECB, in 2008, the rate of inflation will rise from 2.1, this year, to 2.5 per cent, but in 2009 it will fall to 1.9.
According to analysts, the 12-month inflation rate remains around 3 percent, however, the next 3 to 4 months, the annual average rate will be 2.1 percent.
At the same time, they expect the ECB to lower the policy rate twice in 2008.
Gallup points to a government crisis
After a long stagnation, the number of supporters of Fidesz (Alliance of Young Democrats) has increased significantly at the beginning of December. Thus since 2002, it currently has the largest number of supporters, while Gallup (Polling Institute) has never seen such low socialist support, namely 13 percent.
For faithful voters, the difference would represent, due to the greater determination of opposition voters, support of more than two-thirds (71 percent) against the support of a fifth (20 percent) for the MSZP (Hungarian Socialist Party).
According to the poll, the MDF (Forum of Hungarian Democrats) and the SZDSZ (Alliance of Free Democrats) are below the threshold of parliamentarians: their support is two percent in the entire population.
On loyal voters some to vote, the number of supporters of both parties has increased by 1 percent.
The economic climate has continued to deteriorate compared to the previous lowest point, the proportion of those who have judged that the country's economic situation is particularly serious has never been higher, it amounts to 41 per cent and according to 46 per cent complementary the situation is quite serious.
Following the more optimistic prospects of last spring and summer, families are once again more pessimistic about their financial situation.
For next year, the majority of the population is planning an aggravation and only one tenth is predicting an improvement in the situation.
Last December, 71 per cent of those surveyed, i.e. a majority never seen in previous Gallup polls, judged that the Prime Minister was doing his job rather badly than well.
13 percent of respondents have confidence or a lot of confidence in Ferenc Gyurcsány while 38 percent support Viktor Orbán.
54 percent do not trust the Prime Minister at all and 27 per cent trust the president of Fidesz.
One of the indicators of changing the political situation is the proportion of society believing that dissatisfaction with the Prime Minister can be dealt with without a change of government.
Whereas after the riots last October, 35 per cent of the respondents wanted the government and the Prime Minister to remain in office, currently this rate represents only 20 per cent. The relative majority (33 per cent) estimates that holding new elections would be the solution to this situation.
To the question concerning the intention to vote, 60 per cent of the respondents replied that they would certainly go to vote and the additional 20 percent said that they would probably go to vote.
To make the comparison, for a "legislative election to organize next Sunday", only 55 percent of the respondents would certainly participate and 15 per cent complementary would probably participate. According to the current intentions, the result of the referendum would have no doubt.
74 per cent of people would say no to enrollment fees in higher education, 79 per cent would say no to consultation fees and 84 per cent would say no to hospital expenses.
When we look only at the same proportions among those who expressed their intention to vote in the referendum, 81, 84 and 89 per cent of voters respectively would reject the introduction of registration fees, consultation fees, and hospital expenses.
Auchan is the most expensive, Tesco has increased its prices by almost twenty percent
The hypermarkets located in the Budaörs trade triangle maintained the average price increase of 16 percent last year with the difference that this year the VAT rate did not increase.
Article by Napi Gazdaság (Daily Economy)
This year, in Budaörs Commercial Triangel, the usual daily Christmas basket also increased by an average of 16 percent, an increase in value significantly greater than a thousand forints was displayed in all hypermarkets.
Prices, “which had already soared” in food department stores last December, no longer rose sharply compared to the previous high base.
Nevertheless, consumers are obviously shocked to see that items purchased significantly below nine thousand forints last year now cost more than ten thousand forints.
The daily basket in surveyed hypermarkets has exceeded the psychological threshold of ten thousand forints, at least.
And the highest value of the basket amounted to 10 573 forints.
(By 2003, this value was 6,800 forints.)
Unicum and living fish prices remained almost at the level of last year, however prices for turkey, nuts and poppies rose sharply.
In the stores, the price of flour and bread tracked data from KSH (Central Institute of Statistics) but at Auchan bread was found for only 139 forints.
Competition did not lower the price of the product below 200 forints.
It was astonishable to see, also in this hypermarket, that the price of Coca-Cola’s two-liter recorded bottle was below 200 forints, so it cost only 257 forints the recorded bottle included.
Nevertheless, this year, in terms of Everyday basket, Auchan was the most expensive and Cora the cheapest.
According to our calculations, Cora increased the price of her Daily Basket by 15 percent while Tesco and Auchan increased them by about 18 and 18 percent respectively.
Comparing last year's most expensive basket and this year's cheapest basket, we see a 12 percent difference while the difference between last year's cheapest and the most expensive of this year is 21 percent.
Prices increased by 1,480 forints on average.
Last year, prices increased by 1,206 forints on average, while knowing that the impact of the increase in the VAT rate was already noticed in last year's Christmas prices.
This process perplexed trade, hypermarkets could not visibly determine which margin to apply to products as they were unable to predict the impact of price change on consumption.
(If a trader miscalculates the rotation of a product, he risks losing a large profit on the margin adapted to the intensity of trade.)
Due to the change of the VAT rate, the increase in the prices of the Daily Shopping Cart evolved so excessively that the most expensive basket was 1 720 forints than the value of 2006 while the difference between the cheapest baskets was only 844 forints.
This year, the difference was not so excessive since the value of the most expensive basket was greater than 1,630 forints than last year's and the prices of the cheapest also increased by 1,284 forints.
As we approached the two Christmas seasons, we’ve seen a catastrophic price increase, in less than 20 months the prices of everyday consumer items have risen by more than 30 percent in hypermarkets.
(This does not necessarily confirm KSH data: for some basic necessities, the Institute of Statistics has observed a price increase of more than 30 percent in 12 months.
This is the case, for example, flour and egg.)
According to the daily basket of the latter, this seems almost absurd since the level of price of this product, already very expensive last year, has increased by just more than 10 per cent compared to the base.
According to the indices, flour suppliers occupy a stronger position than egg suppliers because they have managed to accept the sharp increase in prices also by the multinationals.
In the commercial golden triangle, hypermarkets don't complain, they constantly record good years.
According to our experiences, the majority of customers no longer look at prices in the three hypermarkets visited.
They buy everything in quantity, they take long-preserved food by pallets.
On Wednesday morning, important queues formed at the crates of the three hypermarkets because the number of customers increased abruptly.
However, according to our information, turnover is less important in the provinces, many multinationals complain among polling companies not even reaching the expected turnover, not only for food but also for sustainable consumption items.
Many hospitals save on disinfectants
This year, more than a thousand infections, caused mainly by the incorrect use of antibiotics, have been recorded in hospitals.
Hygienic conditions of hospitals, insufficient number of beds, overwork of medical staff do not help to block infections, says the chief physician of the National Center for Epidemiology.
Many hospitals also make the economy on disinfectants
Not long ago an MRSA infection was diagnosed in the trauma department at János Hospital.
Antibiotic-resistant bacteria have been detected on a man hospitalized following a serious accident.
The patient has been isolated.
At the beginning of the year a similar infection occurred in the same place.
The injured of a serious car accident came out of the hospital but soon after he had to return due to an MRSA infection and, since then, doctors have not been able to do him an important operation because of the bacterium in his body.
Until 10 December this year, 1,094 hospital infections generated by a multidrug-resistant pathogen have been reported to the National Nosocomial Surveillance System, said Karolina Böröcz, chief medical officer of the National Centre for Epidemiology.
It is the number of infections caused by a multidrug-resistant pathogen that has actually been recorded in hospitals and for the rest we have no information.
Approximately two-thirds of infections (683 infections) were caused by MRSAs, i.e. methicillin-oxacillin-resistant staphylococcus aureus.
One-third of those people carriant for Staphylococcus aureus (SA) bacteria in their noses without developing a disease.
Infections caused by SA (such as angines, tonsillitis, skin infections, traumatic infections) react well to antibiotics, they are easily curable.
However, if antibiotics are used excessively or inappropriately, the bacterium, which responds well to antibiotics, will develop an antibiotic-resistant bacterium that will proliferate rapidly in poor hospital conditions.
In case of temporary or prolonged malfunction of the immune system, this bacterium can cause serious hospital infections, such as traumatic infection or sepsis, on the elderly patients, of small weight or having a weakened organism.
According to the medical director of János Hospital, there is nothing special in MRSA infections, these infections are part of the daily life of hospitals.
We should not confuse the infection with the epidemic, we do not find MRSA only or we do not look for them, said Tibor Nyulasi.
SAs are resistant to antibiotics.
"These patients are insulated, caregivers wear rubber gloves and protective masks and we have suitable antibiotics to treat them," Nyulasi said.
A priori, hospitalized patients are examined if they carry MRSA, however infection cannot always be prevented.
Sample collection is not fashionable
The vast majority of MRSA infections could be prevented, but the current conditions and circumstances are not favourable in Hungarian hospitals to prevent the development and proliferation of multidrug-resistant pathogens, says Karolina Böröcz.
As this infection occurs mainly in hospitals and seniors' residences, hospitals should control hospitalized patients and immediately isolate patients with MRSA.
However, microbiological sampling is not fashionable in Hungarian hospitals.
It should be noted that the National Social Security Fund does not fund these examinations.
Most cases occur only if MRSA infection is detectable on the patient, said the chief physician of the epidemiological center.
The European Union has rigorous recommendations on the appropriate use of antibiotics in human medicine and there are also Hungarian guidelines for the cure of certain infections and syndromes.
Efforts must be made to ensure that antibiotic therapy is targeted, i.e. microbiological examinations should be carried out in order to prevent drug resistance, but hospitals do not always take this into account.
Microbiological sampling is even rarer in ambulatory care and basic care, said Karolina Böröcz.
Many hospitals save on disinfectants
Scientific evidence shows that MRSA proliferates from one patient to another most often through medical personnel.
It is therefore essential to wash your hands, to put on gloves and protective masks. However, significant gaps are detected in hospitals also in this area.
MRSAs proliferate by inhalation of droplet inhalation and contact. However, due to conditions in Hungarian hospitals, the infected patient cannot always be isolated.
In addition, rooms are often full, beds are often too close to each other while in terms of the epidemic, the patients should be away from each other at least 1.5 meters.
Unfortunately, we also find that hospitals, in a difficult financial situation, save on disinfectants, they lack nurses, the patients are numerous, so the risk of contamination is even greater, said Karolina Böröcz.
According to Karolina Böröcz, in hospitals where preventive measures are respected, the number of infections is less demonstrably or else the proliferation of the pathogen can be blocked.
Government project against MRSA
The treatment of MRSA infection represents exorbitant expenses for social security coffers, which is why this infection is affected everywhere.
In England, for example, the government has established a program to prevent or reduce the incidence of MRSA.
According to published data, this programme is effective and MRSA infections show a decreasing trend in England.
The European Centre for Disease Prevention and Control (ECDC) raises among its priorities the prevention of the incidence of multidrug-resistant pathogens (such as MRSA) and the prevention of hospital infections caused by these pathogens.
The commissioner, the author of a fatal accident, was not intoxicated
The official finding of the fatal accident caused by the commissioner of the 22nd arrondissement has been drawn up.
It may be excluded that the commissioner of the 22nd arrondissement, resigned from his post since, who crushed a pedestrian by causing his death last Tuesday, would have driven in a state of drowsiness or dizzy, said Friday Attila Morvai, spokesman of the Public Prosecutor's Office of the capital after the relative observation has been established.
The finding confirmed the first result of the investigation which has already found that the former commissioner had not consumed alcohol before driving
Last Tuesday, the former head of the police station of the 22nd arrondissement crushed a 55-year-old man who found himself in front of him when he turned, with his personal car, in Kossuth Lajos street of the 22nd arrondissement. The man wanted to cross the road not through the pedestrian crossing.
(Moreover, the fact that he was crossing the road outside the pedestrian crossing does not constitute a mitigating circumstance, according to the Highway Code a car that initiates a turn must let pedestrians pass.)
Pedestrians died after being taken to hospital.
As a result of this accident, the commissioner resigned from his position and asked for his retirement because, according to the communication of the police, this accident upset him greatly.
The investigation into this case is being carried out by the Budapest Public Prosecutor's Office.
Attila Morvai also mentioned that the former Commissioner cooperated from the beginning with the magistrates in charge of conducting the investigation.
An additional 400 million euros for infrastructure
János Veres, Hungarian Minister of Finance, and Marta Gajecka, Vice-President of the European Investment Bank (EIB), signed three agreements worth a total of 400 million euros for a line of credit on Friday in Budapest to support education, transport and environmental infrastructure as well as energetics.
In 2006, the European Investment Bank (EIB) adopted a budget of 300 million euros for the Hungarian budgetary financing of transport and environmental projects to be carried out from the Cohesion Fund, of which a credit agreement worth 100 million euros has already been signed by the parties.
The appropriation agreement of 150 million euros also concerns the budgetary financing of projects related to education.
The EBI has approved a total sum of 300 million euros for Hungary, the remaining 150 million euros will be able to be used later, following the extension of the credit agreement.
The parties have signed a contract of 50 million euros for innovation, the state budget will use this envelope in the first place as part of the research and development project to be carried out at the University of Debrecen.
During the negotiations, the Metro Line 4 project was also discussed.
The parties agreed that they would rediscuss the possible amendment of the initial contract when Hungary finalised the details of metro funding with the EU.
According to János Veres, this could be done in the first quarter of 2008.
Since 1990, the EIB has granted a total of 8.4 billion euros for the financing of 113 projects in Hungary.
The EIB grants its appropriations according to EURIBOR's interest rate, with a grace period of 8 years and with no commitment fee.
Bulgaria, a paradise for the EU real estate market
The evolution of the Bulgarian real estate market is spectacular, the attention of the whole of Europe is turned towards this Balkan country little cited in the past.
What, or and that bought in this market of the EU which is always the cheapest but which will quickly become expensive?
Analysis of Re/Max's Bulgarian Division.
Currently, in real estate, Bulgaria is unquestionably the most fashionable target in Eastern Europe with its ski apartments and houses by the cheap sea.
In the mountains, the most popular regions are Bansko, Borovec, Pamprovo and Vitosa and, by the sea, Albéna, the "Golden Sands", the "Sun Coast", the ancient Sozopol and Nessebar but they are increasingly looking for a building in the Kavarna and Balcik region as well.
According to the analysts of Re/Max Bulgaria, sooner or later, the central region of the country, namely Veliko Tarnovo, Gabrovo, Elena, Triavna, will also arouse the interest of investors and they are also more and more to buy in the cheap corner of Ruse.
Sofia, the capital, offers attractive opportunities as well, shopping and office space promises the highest depreciation rate.
Bulgaria is on the best path to becoming one of the most attractive golf paradises in Europe and thus being a priority destination, after the summer season and the winter season, also in the other two seasons of the year.
More vigilant investors are already buying in large numbers, for example in the corner of Bansko.
According to analysts, the people buying a building in Bulgaria are at the same time looking to change their lives, their way of life.
Most buyers are English but others are coming from France, Belgium, Spain and more and more from Romania.
Maltese and Cypriot investors are also present. At the edge of the Black Sea and in the most reputable ski resorts, we traditionally meet many Russian buyers.
Foreign buyers are divided into three groups, says Georgij Jankov, regional director of Re/Max Bulgaria.
The people who intend to settle buy renovated buildings, at a price ranging between 50 and 100 thousand euros, or dilapidated old houses, at a price ranging from 5 to 15 thousand euros, which are then renovated.
The criteria are easy access and communication possibilities, the proximity of a large city, shops and generally that of the local doctor.
The second group includes buyers of second homes (since last December, Bulgaria is mentioned among the top 10 holiday destinations in Germany).
The third group is made up of commercial investors who build in the hopes of realizing added value in the medium or long term.
The price of buildings in the capital is constantly rising due to increasing demand.
In the European Union, real estate prices are the lowest in Bulgaria. However, in the last 5 years they have increased by 21 percent each year.
Rising real estate prices essentially outweigher the increase in wages.
Fodor and the Six Percent Hungarian
According to the communication of Gábor Fodor, Minister of the Environment and Waters, the meetings of professionals end on Tuesday, however, Wednesday, after the official opening, the negotiations of the ministers on the regime of the international climate after 2012 will continue.
Experts and politicians arriving from 192 countries around the world will discuss the Bali Roadmap, which is supposed to define the efforts to be made after the Kyoto Protocol's emission reduction period until 2012.
At this time, lively discussions are being held in this regard between developing and developed countries.
The U.S. also reported that, for the time being, it does not want to discuss accurate figures, while they were willing to sign an agreement on reducing greenhouse gas emissions from 25 to 40 percent from the 1990 level until 2020.
Another important subject of the conference is to see whether developed countries are committed to providing financial and technological assistance to those countries in need.
An agreement has also been signed on aid to be provided to developing countries.
The assistance fund defined by the Kyoto Protocol will be managed by a 16-member Governing Council probably under the UN Global Environment Facility (GEF), Piac és Profit (Market and Profit) reported.
Six percent of Hungary
On behalf of Hungary, Gábor Fodor, Minister of the Environment and Waters, confirms the EU's ambition to retain its role as flagship in global efforts to protect the climate and encourage the signing of the new international agreement by 2009.
The minister explained that the EU is committed to reducing its greenhouse gas emissions by 20 per cent by 20 per cent compared to the level reached in 1990, regardless of the successful signing of the “Per 2012 Agreement”, and was ready to reduce them by up to 30 per cent if the other major regions of the world and/or developing countries were also ready to make commitments tailored to their responsibility and capabilities.
Gábor Fodor recalled that in 1997, the signatory countries of the Kyoto Protocol targeted in total a reduction of 5.2 per cent and all 15 members of the EU at that time made a commitment on 8 per cent less.
Hungary has made a commitment to reduce greenhouse gas emissions by 6 per cent compared to the level of the period between 1985 and 1987, our country will fulfil its commitment, recalls the press release of the Ministry of the Environment.
The stakes are high in Bali because the long-term international agreement on climate policy must be put in place within two years, otherwise the entry into force of the agreement would certainly be postponed after 2012. In this case, the reduction commitments below the values provided for in the Kyoto Protocol would not be immediately followed by a new international system of emission reduction that has been emphasized in the new report of IPCC.
The reduction in emissions would be delayed and the increase in Earth's average temperature by more than 2 degrees celcius could no longer be avoided which, according to the scientists, would have extremely serious and irrevocable consequences.
The British army is recruiting on YouTube
The units of the British army communicate, on the video sharing site, recordings made during its operations in Iraq and Afghanistan with the aim of making themselves popular.
First of all, it is the British Air Force (RAF) that has become passionate about YouTube: the special teams intervening in Afghanistan have been uploading video footage on the operations against the Taliban since March 2006, the BBC announced.
These recordings, taken using miniature cameras mounted on the helmet, are controlled at Air Force Operations Headquarters in Kandahar and they are then transferred to Londrös where compatriots upload them to the Internet.
The political message is unavoidable
Air force soldiers have already passed 139 sequences on the net by this route and their "chain" has been watched by more than 75 thousand people.
The British Ministry of Defence registered as "defenceheadquarters" in the spring of 2007 and provides videos on operations in Iraq and Afghanistan while the Commonwealth Office and the International Peacekeeping Forces in Iraq (MNFI) also have their own channels on YouTube.
Mission in Afghanistan
According to the initial objective of the Air Force, the videos were switched on the net to recruit. According to the Ministry of Defense, they were also used to make known to the general public the real objectives of the presence of the army abroad.
Propaganda published in this way costs virtually nothing in relation to the usual recruitment advertisements spent on television, communicated to the BBC Gordon Mackenzie, a defence consultant. On the other hand, it also inevitably carries a political message since it justifies in a special form the validity of the military operations decided by the government.
The Americans made a game
The army is annoyed because, apart from the fabricated and censored videos carefully, amateur videos are passed on the sharing site which also present, for example, the deaths of soldiers: in the “official” propaganda films, a little hypocritical, the officers do not avoid talking about the losses but they never present the bloody side of the fight.
Moreover, many videos had already appeared on the net presenting the areas of operations in Iraq and Afghanistan that were carried out on a real mission, but the British army has only recently been excited to load these videos.
The Americans make the recruitment a little differently by using the shooting game America's Army downloadable for free. In this game the player can put himself directly in the place of the soldiers as part of a more or less real simulation.
Noël raffled and doughnuts in ministries
Mónika Lamperth, Minister of Labour, does not seem to be sentimental: instead of celebrating Christmas, she will hold an end-of-year meeting with her collaborators who will be able to say goodbye to the year 2007 by taking doughnuts and coffee.
Another ministry will organize a party with live music, yet another will delight officials with a raffle and offer a drink to create a Christmas atmosphere.
Festivion, Christmas atmosphere, concerts and buffet, thus entertains the power.
The public authorities are also preparing for Christmas.
This year, the biggest celebration of Christmas will be organized by the Ministry of Defense but it is not the employees of the ministry who will be invited.
At Christmas, Orphans, the children of fallen soldiers will receive gifts, for missionary Christmas, the family members of the soldiers currently serving in foreign missions are invited and a press reception will also take place.
The ministry plans a budget of 25 million forints to create the end-of-year atmosphere.
In comparison with the other ministries, the National Development Agency (NFÜ) and the Ministry of Economy and Transport (GKM) will celebrate.
The GKM festival will be held in the House of the Future with a total budget of 4 320 000 forints and, out of the six cent wholesale employees, three hundred and fifty are expected.
During this party, the atmosphere of Christmas will be de rigueur, there will be actors and also a raffle.
NFÜ’s Christmas cost 4 700 000 forints and was organised on Wednesday in the National Justice Council (ILO) building with concerts and dinner.
Renting the room costs a million forints, the rest has been spent on more than four hundred guests.
According to our information, an NFÜ service is invited to another Christmas party that is organized with European money by the National Centre for Economic Development, a company managing tenders.
The building of the Théâtre de la Gaîté has been leased for these purposes.
This information has not been confirmed by MAG Zrt because we have not been able to contact the manager.
Costume isn't mandatory
The ILO building hosted not only the NFÜ but also the Ministry of Justice and Policery which, instead of a Christmas party, organized a ball on the occasion of Saint Luca on 7 December.
The ILO did not make them pay for the use of its rooms.
This ball had five hundred people.
The party began with the minister's words of welcome and the dinner was followed by a dancing evening on live music.
Reply to [origo's] question: the evening outfit was not at all obligatory for this ball.
Ministries of health, labour and local authorities are preparing a sober celebration.
The Ministry of Health will organize a show and a party to its employees, within its walls, for 400 000 forints.
On the other hand, Mónika Lamperth, Minister of Labour, does not officially invite his collaborators to a Christmas party but to an end-of-year working meeting.
One hundred and eighty people are expected who will be invited to have coffee and eat doughnuts, said the press service, the party will cost only 350 000 forints.
Gordon Bajnai, Minister of Local Government, will simply invite his collaborators to have a drink in the aula of the Ministry of Local Authorities and Regional Planning.
The Ministry of Finance (PM) will organize a Christmas party in its large room at which 436 employees are expected.
He plans to spend 2,500 forints per guest including a buffet and a drink.
Since the arrival of János Veres, PM employees celebrate Christmas in the same way every year.
No planned festive atmosphere, the official character is reinforced not only by the presentation of the minister but also by the time of the party taking place in the afternoon.
The Ministry of Agriculture will organize a reception on January 20 to celebrate New Year's Eve, the Christmas party will not take place.
The reception will take place at Vajdahunyad Castle, located at City Wood, and according to the communication of the ministry, 1 000 forints per person are calculated for the one hundred guests.
According to the press service, this is going to be a very simple cocktail to which only foreign diplomats accredited in Hungary will be invited.
These cocktails, organized every year, are started by a few words of welcome from the minister followed by a modest meal.
The Ministry of Foreign Affairs and the Ministry of Education and Culture do not celebrate at all for Christmas, [origo] communicated the respective press services.
The press service of the Ministry of the Environment did not know the price of the official Christmas party.
However, more than four hundred people were invited to the festival held at the Museum of Decorative Art.
Mega strike forces gather
The unions of the League and the National Association of Workers' Councils will constitute, on Friday, their strike commission which will be responsible for coordinating Monday's indefinite strike.
On Saturday, a general protest assembly will be held and Monday, the day of the final vote on the law on health funds, the strike will begin.
This action will certainly cause significant traffic jams because rail traffic will be stopped almost completely and employees of BKV (public transport company) will also strike until 1pm.
The Unions of the league will make known, Friday afternoon, the details of their strike on Monday, organized with the National Association of Workers' Councils.
The strike commission of LIGA - MOSZ will also be constituted, it will serve as coordinator of Monday's actions.
Saturday, a general protest assembly will be held and, from Monday, organizations joining the strike will stop work indefinitely if they fail to reach an agreement with the government.
This means that the date of the end of the strike, from the day of the vote in parliament on the law on health funds, is not defined.
If the National Assembly does not pass the law on health coffers, the trade unions will immediately withdraw the call for a strike.
On the other hand, if the law is passed, the strike commissions will meet and decide on the follow-up.
According to Monday's agenda of the National Assembly, it is likely that the vote on the law on health coffers will not take place until late in the evening, or even at night.
Due to Monday's planned strike, significant traffic jams are planned: the railways will stop work indefinitely and during the morning part of the public transport in Budapest and more than half of the Volán companies are at risk of arrest.
At the same time, at different points across the country, half of the track will also be blocked.
Many unions and civil organizations have joined the call to strike, the list of them is permanently updated on the League's website.
Some organizations report striking indefinitely, others have reported a temporary stoppage of work.
Until Thursday afternoon the MÁV (Hungarian Railways) and the Free Union of railway workers (VDSZSZ) have not managed to reach an agreement on minimum services, but, in the run-up to the Christmas celebrations, more and more are those taking the train.
According to the current communications, the public transport of Budapest will strike from the beginning of service until 1pm, Budapest airport between 7 a.m. and 9 a.m., the Industrial Unions of Electricity and Thermal Energy of the League will make a four-hour strike, the Teachers' Union and the Democratic Union of Teachers called to strike respectively for 2 hours and 2 hours to 8 hours.
The National Association of Physicians will strike throughout the country alternately, the Union of Health and Social Sector Employees (EDDSZ) attached to the SZEF will make a two-hour warning strike.
The most important of the four demands, made by the League, requires the government to withdraw its health reform proposal and submit a new conception to social debate.
The second claim requires that the new method of calculating retirement to be implemented starting next year be introduced in several stages.
The thirth claim wants a guarantee, in terms of retiring before the legal age, which would make it possible to pass into the system the functions that deserve it before 2010.
The fourth reason for the action is the rejection by the Free Union of railway workers (VDSZSZ), attached to the Unions of the League, of the proposal of the Ministry of Economy and Transport concerning secondary railway lines and the expectation of another proposal.
Political Capital: The Hungarian Guard has increased country risk
According to the Risk Analysing Division, the activity of the Hungarian Guard, formed last August, with the support of Jobbik Magyarországért Mozgalom (Movement for a Better Hungary) increases, in several aspects, the political risk of Hungary and the region.
In its “risk warning”, the company points out that, in relation to the activity of the Hungarian Guard, the greatest political risk is already that “in the short term aggressive ethnic clashes can occur as a result of the aggravation of the already existing ethnic tension between Hungary’s Gypsy and non-Gypsy population”.
The research institute added that the Hungarian Guard's political strategy presumably aimed at provoking this situation is the main reason.
As they say, this is explained by one of the main shortcomings of Hungarian political actors: “Public actors have passed the public debate on the Roma affair to the representatives of radical and extreme political groupings who have based a political strategy on the dispute between Gypsies and Hungarians.”
The problem is aggravated, normal dialogue becomes impossible, extremists are strengthened and the arrival of aggressive conflicts is more likely, they say.
However, according to the research institute, under the effect of the increased attention of the Hungarian and international media the activity of the Hungarian Guard "has significantly deteriorated Hungary's image abroad, in particular with regard to confidence in the stability and democratic maturity of the country".
They recall that, following a greater publicity given to the reorganization of Hungarian radical and extreme right-wing groups since the autumn of 2006, many associations have been formed in Hungary since the summer of 2007 calling themselves "National Association of Self-Defense".
"The common feature of these gatherings is that they define themselves as a civilian organization while they publicly declare the preparation of their adherents for defense missions (disasters, national defense, defense of order), armed if necessary, moreover, by referring to the incapacity of the police, the army, in other words of the state," they added.
They pointed out that everything happened according to the method that, based on the resentment of the society of politics and parties, seeks to disguise different political ambitions in a civil aspect.
The emphasis placed on the civil character and the status of an association therefore serves only to avoid the legal pitfalls of the registration of these associations in the court but they are also a political strategy.
The analysis points out that the activity of the Hungarian Guard is a factor that also increases the risk compared to neighbourhood relations.
“In recent months, many neighbouring countries are citing the Hungarian Guard as a potential source of risk and ultranationalist political actors in some neighbouring countries wish to justify their anti-Hungary policy by referring to the constitution of the Hungarian Guard.
This influences the political stability of the region,” they added.
According to the research institute, the constitution of the Hungarian Guard is not a unique phenomenon in Central Eastern Europe, political risks have increased throughout the region.
As they say, the functioning of the Hungarian Guard resembles, for example, the activity of the Bulgarian National Guard whose constitution was declared by the Bulgarian National Union (BNU) in August 2007.
The many Roma unrest that broke out in a neighborhood of Sofia (Kraszna Poljana) are at the origin of the constitution of the Bulgarian Guard.
Taking advantage of these events, the BNU has decided to constitute a guard by saying that the goal of the organization is “national self-defense.”
According to them, over the past 17 years, gypsies have "terrified" Bulgaria but the state has remained inactive and neutral.
They added that the initiative sparked lively debates in Bulgarian public opinion.
As they say, the statement by some Bulgarian Roma organisations regarding the formation of their own guard as resistance signals the increase in the risk of ethnic clashes.
The functioning of the Hungarian Guard showing similarities to that of the Bulgarian National Guard does not rule out that the Hungarian Roma react to the threat in the same way by organizing their own self-defense.
At the request for information of the telegraphic agency, Attila Juhász, research director of Political Capital, said: the risk analysis is one of the activities of the research institute.
As he said, their risk analysis is published every year and if events occurred that could have an impact on the change in risk, they inform public opinion, as in this case, by issuing a risk warning.
The party is not marked in red everywhere
In Hungary, the law defines exactly the holidays and, around the holidays, it has become common to reorganize the working days whose number will decrease next year.
The holidays aren’t uniform in the EU and the US either.
The Hungarian legislation distinguishes the days of national and state holidays as well as the days of rest.
Resting days are often linked to religious holidays or important historical events.
In Hungary, we celebrate the new year, the last day of the year that ends and the first day of the New Year are also days off, the latter all the more so that eavolkers can rest quietly.
Moreover, in a year, we have in all eleven celebrations marked in red.
March 15 is a national holiday, in commemoration of the revolution of 1848, as on October 23, which is the commemorative day of the revolution of 1956.
On August 20, we celebrate the constitution of our state, May 1 is Labor Day and on November 1 and 2, we remember members of our family and deceased friends.
In addition, we have two days at Easter, at Pentecost and at Christmas.
The days of our state celebrations, national or religious rarely falling on a weekend, depending on the calendar, it has become common to reorganize the working days in cases where there is only one working day left before or after the festival marked in red.
It is true that we pay the price of extended weekends by working or going to school on the Saturday before the extended weekend.
For many years, the Minister of Labour has ruled in a special regulation on the replacement days of the days before or after the holidays.
The law extends to all employers and their employees, to civil servants and to persons working in the public service.
It does not, however, apply to service companies, institutions that turn uninterruptively and into service, because of their vocation, and also for days of rest.
This year, the working days will be modified only around the end-of-the-year celebrations: from December 24, life stops almost throughout the country because according to the experiences the majority of people rather overtime or takes a vacation that they have saved for these purposes to be able to spend the days between Christmas and New Year's Day at home.
Next year a lot of parties fall in the middle or at the end of the week, therefore there will be fewer changes in working days compared to this year.
The calendar will be reorganized the first time around Labor Day to allow employees to stay at home four days in a row.
Saturday, April 25 will be a working day to have a day off on Friday, May 2.
Another change is planned for October 23: Saturday, October 18 will be a working day replacing Friday 24.
On the other hand, next year, the end of the year is announced under the sign of the holidays because from December 24, everyone will take a non-stop break even if New Year's Day falls on a Wednesday.
Six futile things that can bother terribly colleagues
Emails that we forget to send, vocal messages we never receive, innocent lies that annoy us almost more: these are things that “beautify” the daily life of a workplace.
The question is whether we get used to these problems or we take up the challenge and we consciously avoid ambiguous situations, causing trouble for others.
examples.
"Excuse me, I forgot to tell you that you've been called from the marketing department," a colleague told you.
That you missed an appointment?
At best he’s sorry and trying to make things right by calling the marketing department to tell them he forgot to pass the message (that’s the least common solution).
In the majority of cases, it is arranged with an apology.
Before you have painful explanations, it's helpful to think about how you can cause unpleasant moments to your colleagues and make efforts to avoid them.
Are you borrowing something that doesn't belong to you?
There's nothing more annoying than wanting to take a file, an office tool or the phone and you can't find them anywhere.
Do you remember that the day before you put the stapler on the desk, but she disappeared the next morning?
Do you accidentally find your pen that you thought were lost on your colleague's desk?
Don't take anything from your co-workers without asking otherwise they're right to be angry with you for stinging their property.
Don't bring envelopes, post-it in your pocket because it can be annoying that there's no more and you need them right now.
Are you chatting about the private lives of the co-workers?
There is no good way to stop gossip spreading.
Who did what, with whom?
Or and why?
Don't tell everyone your information (suppositions) about the privacy of your colleagues!
If a co-worker shares his intimate secrets with you, don't abuse his confidence!
Bury within yourself the shared information and don't discuss it with your colleagues in his absence even if your colleagues also know.
Do you declare yourself sick without just cause?
When you call the office and you declare yourself sick under the pretext of a heartbreaking headache because you feel bad or you think you need rest that day, think of the fact that your work, your urgent affairs, your future missions must be performed by someone else in your place.
Don't hurt your colleagues.
If you know in advance that the next day you won't go to work or that something can happen that would force you to stay at home, don't forget to warn your leader and your co-workers to prevent them from being surprised by your absence the next day.
Hedging, sneering, telephone
You immerse yourself in your work but the sneering of your co-workers pulls you away from it abruptly?
Didn't you, unwittingly, witness a phone conversation that you'd better not listen to?
Don’t bother your colleagues with hummings, chantoning, aloud discussions (which you lead over their heads), footbeats, dirty words or displeasure expressed aloud.
They can disturb even if your colleagues are not immersed in a project (writing, design, organization).
Are you accusing others for a mistake?
If your work is not done for the set deadline, you forget to send an important letter or message, does not accuse anyone for this forgetfulness!
Don't put it on the account of the possible chaos in the office or your noisy colleagues!
Recognise it if you made a fault and if it presented inconveniences for others, fix the mistake!
Ask how you could fix your fault, fix negligence!
You're feeling too much at home at the office?
Putting on a jog and slippers is comfortable at home but they are not suitable for the office!
Don't wear comfortable jogging even if your function allows it!
Don’t be neglected, respect your colleagues and yourself by dressing properly, and if your function demands it by putting on pretty and elegant clothes, to go to work!
If you want to meet expectations, you're not interesting anymore
We're moving slowly in the usual morning plug.
Suddenly, a particular melody is heard on the radio: the voice of a violin with which electronic effects are associated.
I'll raise the sound.
The music changes its rhythm and the bass arrives to accompany the tones later, then a female choir comes to join like a real jewel.
Mr2 airs Zagar's song Wings of Love.
The Hungarian musical life has not spoiled us for a long time with a good quality electronic pop.
However, now it seems that the cork becomes different if you listen to Zagar's new album.
The appearance of Yonderboi, the few interesting new productions born of the Hungarian digital underground are gradually beginning to change the overall image and, despite the new fashion of garage rock tearing the guitar, the Hungarian electropop proves that there is something new under the sun.
Balázs Zságer arrived from Pécs and played himself in Yonderboi’s group before he embarked on his own path, perhaps because “there’s no room for two feet in the same shoe.”
His project (Zagar) and his music, an alloy of jazz, electronic dancing music and pop, began to make himself known when he was entrusted with the composition of the filmed soundtracks (e.g.
Ferenc Török's season).
The line-up starting in small clubs began to be known by a wider audience when Wan2 magazine cited their first album of 2002 among the fifty most important records on the Hungarian market and proclaimed Zagar, with Yonderboi, the almost only creators of the Hungarian trend who would also be competitive in the west.
Zagar and his whole unquestionably "trended" but no one asked them if they wanted to wear this label.
The group reacted properly, it released a new and better record.
The recently released Cannot Walk Fly Flaister album can open new avenues for them, although the title wishes to represent continuity with the years spent in Pécs.
It was a line from the former group of Pécs de Balázs Zságer.
We are well there with the reference to flying but next to the aerial music appears now, following the spirit and trend of the time, the stronger guitar, impact of rock and roll.
György Ligeti, singer currently working in England with the band The Puzzle, showed his talent in these songs during the premiere of the album at the Millennium Park.
On the album, we find a real hit for radio, mr2 Petõfi, recently broadcasting popular music from morning to night, began to introduce the melodies of Wings of Love recorded with six Hungarian singers ("Underground Divas").
It's all right? (?).
hvg.hu asked Baláz Zságer questions.
hvg.hu: This new hit pushes me to ask a question: has your music remained music aimed at a certain layer?
Zságer Balázs: The term of music aiming at a certain layer doesn’t tell me much.
For me there are two castes in light music; not mainstream or underground, non-alternative or pop but commercial music and sincere music.
So-called alternative, underground music can also be mediocre and made only to sell and thus become commercial.
However, a good pop song can also be sincere.
Reception attitude also works in this spirit regardless of language or borders.
hvg.hu: Do you see a difference between the Hungarian and foreign audience, is one or the other more open to your music?
Zs.B.: Abroad, especially in the west, light music has older traditions.
La, people go to concerts and not only the young people of about ten or twenty but also the oldest.
They follow with much more attention the changes that have occurred in light music because they believe that it is also part of contemporary culture.
hvg.hu: What’s the role of the audience in your work?
Are you interested to know who, or how many people are listening to your music?
Zs.B.: I’m obviously happy to see that more and more people come to our concerts.
We have never made music for the market.
For us the music is not made to achieve a goal but for a specific reason.
The role of the public is more important to concerts where mutual influence already works but it is perceived only in the elusive changes of the moment.
However, I noticed that if you wanted to meet the expectations of the audience, you won't be interesting anymore.
hvg.hu: Are you planning to follow Yonderboi’s example?
He worked alone and had a career in the west.
Zs.B.: We don’t really follow his path even if sometimes some try to find traces in our music.
Instead, we’re team players who have confidence in each other’s musical presence and let them unfold.
At first, it was of course unavoidable that our music would be compared to Yonderboi because many of us leave his band and take another path.
hvg.hu: On mr2 Petõfi, Wings of Love ranks first.
Many have heard Zagar's name for the first time through this song.
With this more popular style you consciously opened towards a wider layer?
Zs.B.: We didn’t plan to make a tube to be able to sell the disc.
This song means more things.
We wanted it for the end of the album to try to soften the orgy of sounds and the more difficult themes tackled throughout the record.
hvg.hu: How did you choose all six singers?
Why do they - what was the guideline?
Zs.B.: The idea was to have a choir like gospel.
We had the idea to compose this choir of good soloists from the Hungarian music scene.
Thus the six-member choir was composed, namely Sena, Edina Kutzora, Judie Jay, Bori Péterfy, Enikõ Hodosi [Neo], Juci Nemeth, which was later called Underground Divas.
hvg.hu: Did you want this song like that or did the girls change it a bit?
Zs.B.: This track already existed for a long time in an instrumental version and then when we composed the album, we thought there was still something missing from this song.
The suite of chords drew the voice of the song.
I sang the same melody that the girls later learned.
I got it almost immediately and everything was terribly spontaneous.
I remember that it galvanized me at the time but of course we needed the Divas.
With my voice she wouldn’t have the same strength.
hvg.hu: On the record and at the concert also it seemed to me that the girls were in the background.
There’s no solo (with the exception of a short Judy Jay solo), they don’t have a role alone, they all sing together and they don’t sing louder than the music, so the music doesn’t just accompany their song.
They were back on the stage, too.
Is it wanted?
Zs.B.: The fact that they were in the background is solely due to technical problems.
On the other hand, what was voluntary is that we did not want to distribute soloist roles.
The song also says that we have to forget a bit about our ego, forget who comes from where, who goes or, we just have to let that these wings, the wings of love, take us away.
I wanted others to also feel this euphoric state that we felt when the song was born.
hvg.hu: Which songs made you work the most?
Zs.B.: Actually, none as to the process of musical creation, we had more difficult pieces during mixing.
For example, with Dorian Gray's Dilemma, where I play a concert piano, or with Rock'n'Roll Goes To The Girls, or the groove didn't want to work for a long time, and then, little by little, everything was set up like in a puzzle.
hvg.hu: What's your favorite on the new album?
Zs.B.: It changes all the time with the concerts and the fact that I have already “let go” this record.
It’s Prophet Is A Fool, Escape From The Earth and Never The Same.
Treastly trader to risk billions because of its inferiority complex
A concealer fraudster.
Thus its former employee is the French giant Societe Generale, owner of the Czech bank Komerční banka.
The bank has lost nearly five billion euros because of it.
However, it seems rather that Kerviel is only a great player who wanted to match his colleagues, and who, in addition, cannot be considered incapable.
Unlike all the major bankhouses, he acknowledged in time the U.S. Mortgage market crisis.
"He's fragile," his superiors, who denounced him to the police.
However, if we stick to Kerviel's deposition reported by the French media, including Le Monde, this man's transactions produced at the end of last year a profit amounting to 1.6 billion euros.
Crisis is Beyond the United States
"All I wanted was to make money for my bank," he said.
Last summer, he managed to take advantage of the American crisis to earn half a billion euros.
In fact, he felt the opportunity at the beginning of the year.
Reports began to emerge in February that so-called "sub-prime" mortgages granted to low-income customers or those who had encountered repayment difficulties in the past would have problems.
However, this crisis should not affect the entire economy.
Kerviel didn't believe it, and he bet well.
Thus, at the end of the year, its profits amounted to 1.6 billion euros.
"As soon as I won my first half-billion, I didn't know how to announce it," Kerviel says and adds that he has, of course, kept nothing for himself."
Throughout the interrogation, he admits to having distorted the reports so as not to be detected.
He managed to fool his superiors, although the Eurex exchange began to take an interest in his transactions.
Who doesn’t risk anything has nothing
Is he afraid of being discovered?
Rather not.
"I felt that the mere fact of having obtained 1.6 billion for the bank would satisfy them."
Where does his desire to risk so big come from?
He has reached his position only gradually.
Had started working at Societe Generale in 2000 just after completing his studies at the University of Lyon.
His annual salary was around 51 thousand dollars.
Two years later, he was already a trading assistant and, in 2005, he became an independent trader with an annual salary of 90 thousand dollars.
However, he knew he would never earn as much as others.
"From my first interview in 2005, I knew that I was much less considered than the others.
In view of my university curriculum and my professional and personal background," Kerviel told investigators.
However, shortly after taking office, he achieved his first great success.
Thanks to Allianz shares, he gained half a billion euros by betting on the decline of this stock during the attacks in Londrès.
And the mechanism was triggered - he wanted more.
As long as you're wining, we'll leave you alone
"There was like a snowball effect," he told the police.
But the superiors were aware of everything, or rather, they suspected.
"As long as I won, they were pretending to close their eyes."
However, it is then that the coup at the beginning of the year comes.
He's losing a billion euros in one day.
In mid-January, after the weekend, he decides to hide the sum.
On Monday, when he arrives at work, he is no longer employed by the bank.
A few days later, the bank announces that it has lost 5 billion euros because of him.
And how did we find out about it?
He's become a suspect because of his holidays.
"Last year, I took only 4 days off.
A trader who doesn’t take a vacation is a trader who doesn’t want to leave his book with another,” Kerviel concludes.
The Czech Republic has an opportunity to get 365 billion
Yesterday, the ministers of the Czech government signed nine operational programmes with representatives of the European Commission, which could, in the coming years, bring 14 billion euros (approximately 365 billion Czech krona) to the Czech Republic.
This is about half of the entire amount that the Czech Republic can obtain from Brussels in the years 2007 to 2013.
Nearly 125 billion crowns from seven operational programmes will go to the Czech regions.
Czech companies will be able to obtain about 100 billion kronor under the Enterprise and Innovation programme.
The transport sector will benefit from the largest share, up to 150 billion.
The Transport programme is the most important operational programme and accounts for up to 22 per cent of the financial resources that Czech Parliament can obtain under these projects.
This money will be at the origin of an increase in the budget of the National Transport Infrastructure Fund which will manage next year a sum of 90.8 billion crowns.
The Enterprise and Innovation programme, aimed at SMEs and entrepreneurs, must be used to obtain financial means to encourage innovation within the company.
Companies should obtain financial means for the introduction of new technologies, research into industry, but also for the introduction of new and more efficient management methods.
Until now, Czech Rep. was one of the new members of the beneficiaries of the less successful EU funds.
The Tribunal upheld the 20-year prison sentence for Nicaragua's ex-president
The Nicaraguan Court of Appeal on Thursday upheld the 20-year prisone sentence for former President Arnold Alemán, to whom he was sentenced in 2003 for a US$100 million (nearly US$1.8 billion kroron).
However, he was later liberated and under house arrest in his hacienda near the capital of Nicaragua.
If the former head of this Central American state, in office between 1997 and 2002, will or will not be incarcerated again is at the moment, according to the AP agency, unclear.
According to the president of the Court of Appeal Ileana Pérez, everything will now depend on the prison agents, or they will let Aleman finish his sentence at home, or go to prison again.
4 years ago, the Tribunal proved that Alemán routinely moved government money to accounts of foreign companies in Panama.
They were fictitious companies and the accounts actually belonged to his family members and his closest supporters.
Part of that money went into the funds Alemán had set up to finance his election campaign in 2001.
We've adopted the budget
That's how it is.
The state budget has been adopted.
How is this budget exceptional?
It is the first budget designed by this government and accepted by the government majority without the support of the opposition.
The one for the current year passed a year ago thanks to the support of the Czech Socialist Party - ČSSD, since it was Minister Sobotka who had prepared it and ČSSD could not afford his refusal.
Contrary to the turbulent debate preceding the vote of the declaration of mistrust to the government, this time, nothing dramatic.
The Chamber of Deputies adopted without any problems this law which, although the most influential, is usually neglected.
That's some kind of paradox.
Whether we like it or not, each chapter and every article is the beginning and the end of any government.
The budget is part of politics, although hidden behind the competition of power between government and opposition.
The latter is more attractive in the media and that's why she's given more attention in the media.
Politician disputes are of much more interest to opinion than abrupt figures.
The national budgets of past socialist governments suffered from three evils that the current budget is not able to settle at the same time:
The first being the large part granted to the mandate fees imposed by law, constituted not only by pensions, but also by social charges, adopted last year by the silent "coalition" bringing together the ČSSD and KSČM parties.
The second is a deficit economy, as a result of the first evil.
The third hurdle is the deficit of public finances, i.e. the deficit of cities and municipalities.
However, it is not the deficit in the state budget that represents the greatest hazard.
It is public and relatively under control.
The real time bomb is the deficit of cities and municipalities.
Many mayors often issued, in dizziness, bonds, disproportionately indebting their municipalities, in order to obtain, apart from money from taxes, tasks and bank loans, new sources of investment.
In previous years, they managed to repay these debts through the mass sale of shares of distribution systems, especially those of energy, obtained from the state in the context of privatizations.
They no longer have this source.
If one sticks only to official and verifiable facts, we find that:
Our economy has already been going through for several years, like the rest of the world, a phase of growth and ČSSD does not fail to wield it.
It was a unique opportunity for the successive governments of this party to regularize public finances.
However, in place of that, they were going into more and more in debt.
Other countries, apart from a few exceptions such as Hungary, Albania or Egypt, managed their affairs in a much more reasonable way than our republic.
It is a monstrous disgrace that essentially falls on previous governments.
We are one of the countries that, on a global scale, are the less threatened by poverty.
We therefore do not need massive social programs which have, precisely in recent years, unfortunately unnecessarily swollen.
Although some of the absurd populist spending, approved last year before the elections, has been eliminated if an age limit shift for retirement, as well as a reform of the pension system will not take place soon, then any policy will cease to exist in this country and whoever will be in power, it will only administer.
By barely exaggerating, it can be said that politicians in power will become bureaucrats mechanically distributing the majority of the money imposed between pensions and social benefits.
That is why the current budget cannot be revolutionary, but it can only suspend the mechanism which means that the ordinary costs are postponed by mandate costs.
The 70-billion deficit projected for 2008 would be absolutely useless if previous governments hadn’t dissipated all the money they could.
If we really don't want to happen that policies in power become mere bureaucrats, we need to be patient and give this fragile government coalition, aware that the state can only spend the equivalent of what it manages to levy on taxes and tax rights, the calm necessary for the preparation of new reform laws.
There are only the latters that will gradually achieve a balanced state budget.
Jiří Krejčí
The banks want to solve the crisis
The U.S. Federal Reserve Bank, the European Central Bank and the English, Swiss and Canadian central banks have decided to fight the financial market crisis together.
More than one hundred billion dollars will thus be invested in money markets through auctions.
It will be a question for banks to sell, through an auditing system, interest rates from which they are willing to borrow money.
For example, the U.S. Fed will auction US$40 billion and, in addiction, it will provide 24 billions to the European and Swiss Central Banks.
This is the first time since the attacks of 11 September that the Central Banks of Individual States have decided on action at such a concerted point, aimed at preventing or even diminishing the effects of the financial crisis.
“This approach tends to solve the major problems of the economy, i.e. the growing lack of free capital that banks could lend,” writes Bernard Baumohl of the consulting firm Economic Outlook Group.
“Conclusive action by central banks has diminished the likelihood of a recession in the United States from 65 percent to about 50 percent,” Baumohl said.
Banks have already lost US$60 billion because of unrepaid loans, especially in the United States.
Analysts are still waiting for billions of losses.
"If the central banks have chosen this approach, it is because they have to really understand what can still ensue," says ABN chief economist Amro Kieran Davies.
"It seems that the situation is really bad," he added.
Central banks are concerned that if the banks themselves have difficult access to loans, they will lend their customers more dearly.
This would decrease consumption and plunge the U.S. economy into a recession that could affect economic growth around the world.
The Central Banks made this choice after we failed to bring down London's interbank rate, called LIBOR, used to borrow on the interbank market.
This meanned that banks were still afraid of mutual borrowings, although the U.S., Canadian and English Central Banks repeatedly lowered their interest rates during the fall.
"This will have the same effect as a further fall in interest rates," Greg Salvagggio of Tempus Consulting told Reuters.
Some analysts do not believe that the Central Banks approach will not contribute to conjuring the crisis, since it does not solve the main problem which is the fall of the housing market in the United States.
President Klaus: the debates of environmentalists are unbelievable
Global climate change is believed to be primarily detrimental to developing countries.
President Václav Klaus spoke again about the issue of global warming.
Criticism this time hit the United Nations International Conference on Climate Change ending in Bali.
In Vienna, where he presented his book The Blue Planet, not green, he stated that the debates of environmentalists were incredible.
According to Klaus, it is not only the structure of the conference, made up of a curious mixture of representatives of governments and non-governmental organizations, which is unacceptable, but also the basic difference between accompanying rhetoric and reality.
"The debate isn't structured at all, it's just a rocket of words, using solutions to current problems," Klaus said.
During the presentation of his book, the Czech president stressed that his subject is of great importance to him and that is why he is so committed to this cause.
He also expressed his satisfaction that his book also appears in German translation, since, he said, "I often encounter only the caricature of my opinions".
From now on, interested persons can read his positions without them being distorted.
Klaus recalled that although he is not a climatologist, he nevertheless, in his opinion, has enough provisions to write such a book.
He is indeed an academicist able to follow and appreciate scientific treatises, he has the practice of statistics and he is also an economist.
The major conclusions of the book are, according to him, the following theses: the climate is constantly evolving, so the changes are normal, there is not an opinion shared by all researchers on global warming, the effects of the current changes are neither too important nor too serious, they therefore represent no danger and, finally, the efforts carried out in order to influence the evolution of the climate are useless, ineffective and unnecessarily costly.
All the more since he has the experience of a totalitarian regime, he considers it unacceptable to impose unverified views on others, which he feels as a dangerous attack on freedom.
In response to questions from those present, he repeatedly explained that it was not against "reasonable protection of the environment, but against fundamentalist environmentalism that does not take into account the relationship between the fees and the profit they bring".
In Vienna, Klaus had already talked about this topic two months ago at the Hayek Institute.
600 thousand people have failed to renew their driver's license on time
Six hundred thousand drivers allowed the deadline to expire and failed to renew their former driver's licence, the validity of which expires at the end of the year.
We are the last day when people can still apply for renewal, so that the authorities are able to issue them a new permit before the end of the year.
However, the Department is not afraid that hundreds of thousands of drivers without a valid licence will take the road.
According to the authorities, have not renewed their driver's license especially those who no longer wish to drive.
As municipalities report a decline in the number of licence renewal applications, authorities in the capital are overwhelmed with applications and the number of licence renewal applications rose this week.
The Town Hall satisfies approximately 2000 customers per day.
There's about half an hour tail.
In Prague, nearly 140.OOO drivers have not yet renewed their driver's licenses.
Issuing a new licence takes 20 days.
But it is possible to request the delivery within a shortened period of five days.
In this case, the driver pays a surcharge of five hundred crowns.
Drivers of vehicles who will not be able to carry out the mandatory renewal of the driver's licence by the end of the year and will take the road without a valid licence, will risk, as early as January, a fine.
The culprit will be forced to pay a maximum of two thousand crowns.
However, the police officer can also deal with the offence using an amicable approach.
In the case of an administrative offence, the fine climbs to 2500 krones.
According to previous information, was liable to a fine even a person who was not going to circulate.
In doing so it could be forced to pay up to 30,000 kroons.
The Ministry had called on the authorities for moderation and imposing fines not going beyond 1000 crowns.
However, according to the spokesman of the Ministry of Transport Karel Hanzelka, no one risks fines in tens of thousands.
According to him, the driver's license is a document that people can decide whether they wish to have it or not.
It's not like with the identity card that has to be valid without exceptions.
People who no longer want to drive should hand over their driver’s license.
You just have to bring it or send it to the corresponding municipality.
Driver's licences issued between 1964 and 1993 will cease to be valid at the end of the year.
However, vehicle drivers are also forced to progressively renew other types of driving licences.
Individuals with documents dating from the years 1994 to 2000 still have three years to carry out the renewal.
The validity of driving licences issued in the years 2001 to 2004 expires in December 2013.
According to Hanzelka, this is about 2.6 million other documents.
The Tribunal has reduced the sentences of detectives placed with Berdych
Josef Opava and Petr Koňařík, former police officers accused of colluding David Berdych's gang, will do thirteen and ten years in prison respectively.
The Superior Court of Pragua has thus definitively sentenced them by reducing their sentences by 1 year and 2 years respectively.
Originally, the Department's investigators for the fight against organized crime faced sentences of 14 and 12 years in prison.
It is no longer possible to appeal against the judgment pronounced today, only an appeal to the Superior Tribunal is possible.
Although Berdych is also accused in this case, he awaits for the moment only the verdict of first instance.
However, he has already received sentences in other trials, the sum of which exceeds 16 years in prison.
He can't receive more.
In January, the Departmental Court found guilty for participation in 19-persoons, the Superior Tribunal was now dealing with the interjections of appeal of 16 of them.
Most of the indictees, since the beginning of the investigation, questioned the accusation by claiming that it was a manipulated case.
According to the Central Bohemian Court of Justice, members of the police, after an agreement with Berdych among others, provided criminals with information from police sources, covered the various hold-ups and helped gang members avoid criminal liability.
The gag returned 30 per cent of the larcine to Opava and Koňařík.
In the accusation, there is talk of the criminal activity of the gang in the years 1999 to 2001.
Essentially armed robbery whose victims have, in most cases, suffered a serious attack on health, but also the abuse of power of a public official and prohibited armaments.
During home raids, the police, in fact, discovered illegally detained pistols, shells with a steel core, a viewfinder for direct laser shooting or a machine gun.
According to the charges, the gang has been enriched with tens of millions of kronors.
Apart from nearly twenty men of this trial, the courts have already found guilty of other robberies Berdych and a whole series of other people.
Other men in Berdych's neighborhood are still explaining to each other in court in another trial, some cases have not yet reached the court.
For the time being, Tomáš Půta and Maroš Šulej, who are currently living in detention in Ireland, where they are awaiting the final decision regarding their extradition to the Czech Republic.
The price of child substitution: 12 million
The lawyer of the affected families Igor Veleba wants to obtain from Třebíč hospital a compensation of 12 million crowns plus costs.
Three million for each of mothers, two million for fathers and one million for each child.
The hospital offers a maximum of 200,000 for each parent.
That's why Ondřej Dostál Hospital's lawyer absolutely disagrees with Veleba's proposal.
"We reject such a claim, it is very very high," Dostál said at the end of the hearing.
"In order to be able to form an opinion on the counter-proposal, we need the expert report commissioned by the opposing party.
We're going to see if it has any explanatory value.
But we continue to believe that the total amount should not exceed hundreds of thousands, "said Dostál.
According to him, the amount should be fixed between 100,000 and 200,000 Kč for each of the four parents.
At the beginning of the case, Jabloňov's family demanded a million crowns for each month when she could not raise her biological daughter.
Veleba used the expert report, written for him by the University Hospital in Prague-Motol, as a supporting document for the compensation negotiations.
According to experts in psychology and psychiatry, parents suffered psychological damage and were prone to stress at different scales and depths.
The situation of stress has been better endured by men, although they have been confronted with remorse of not having been able to prevent the substitution of newborns.
Women remain less serene in front of the experience of trauma in the news and in front of what is happening precisely at the moment, summarized the contents of the Veleba report.
Veronika and Nikola were replaced by nurses at Třebíč Hospital on 9 December.
Last week, the children returned to their biological parents - Nikola with the Čermák in Přibyslavice and Veronika with Libor Brož and Jaroslava Trojanová in Jabloňov.
At the end of October, the Governor of the Vysočina Miloš Vystrčil handed to each 100,000 kroron families for the reimbursement of the expenses caused by the error of the Třebíč hospital managed by the region.
All hospitals in the Czech Republic are obliged by law to provide civil liability insurance.
In case of failure, they have to draw on the bottom of the reserve, exceptionally, they can ask for help from the manager.
Until now the courts recognized relatively low compensation, the sums calculated according to the tables were of the order of hundreds of thousands, exceptionally millions.
Polívka lost Valašské Království (the Kingdom of Valašsko)
Bolek Polívka losed the dispute over the Valašské království brand (Kingdom of Valašsko).
According to the judge of the Ostrava Regional Court, it was indeed he who had used for the first time the title King of Valašsko, but the project was set up by the team around Tomáš Harabiš, former collaborator of the actor.
Polívka wasn't present at today's hearing.
However, according to his lawyer, the case is probably not finished and his client will appeal.
"The dispute concerns the fact that Mr. Harabiš and his team parasitize on Bolek Polívka's popularity," Polívka's lawyer said after the trial.
According to him, the words Kingdom of Valašsko evoke to everyone precisely this actor and comedian.
Harabiš agrees.
"There's a job of almost ten years behind us.
Looking for money and developing events," he said.
According to him, money is the cause of litigation.
"After years, they realized that the project is successful and that they could take advantage of it.
It’s those who want to parasitize on our work,” he added.
A lucrative business
According to the court, it was Polívka who used for the first time the title valašský král (King of Valašsko) in his television show.
Actor Radoslav Brzobohatý crowned him king in 1993.
However, at the time, this had nothing to do with the plan to set up a fictitious kingdom.
A few years later, Harabiš came with the idea of making Valašské Království’s passports appear.
From a humorous action at the beginning there was a business and a lucrative commercial activity, followed by the creation, by Harabiš, of Valašské království.
In 1997, Polívka accepted that his name and signature should be mentioned in the passport and he even offered the holders sales on the price of visiting his farm and theatre shows.
Which is going to sit on the throne?
Today, the judge also mentioned that Harabiš only used the bare idea, published by Polívka on Manéž, for commercial purposes.
"The popularity of Boleslav Polívka certainly helped the Valašské království project," the judge said.
She added, however, that the soul of the project consisted of Harabiš and its team, which devoted themselves to the project intensely.
The collaboration between today's enemies continued until 2000 when Harabiš organized an official coronation for Polívka in Vsetín.
But from there, conflicts began to accumulate between Polívka and Harabiš, which culminated with the deposition of "King Boleslav 1st elected forever".
The leading role in the kingdom was then, under the inspiration of Harabiš, assumed by singer Jarmila Šuláková as Queen Mother.
Then, in 2002, Polívka filed a complaint against Harabiš and his company requesting that the court have today rejected.
What could clear up the matter is the tournament envisaged for the throne and one-half of the princess.
He'll get a new king out of it.
He didn’t want to betray the details and the date yet.
“We don’t want to go fast.
It would be something like the parade of kings in Slovácko.
The king would be elected for some time.
Even Mr. Polívka can of course register, "added Harabiš.
Peugeot 207 SW 1.6 VTi test: disappearance of prejudice
In fact, I’ve never been a big fan of the Peugeot 206.
Its rolling qualities were nothing extraordinary, the quality of the change of speed, of driving and also that of manufacturing could, in many respects, be described as less than average.
However, currently there is on the market its successor the Peugeot 207, which is much better.
Especially since the combi named SW still goes one step further, I just have to think better.
When I was testing the classic hatchback of the Peugeot 207 I complained, for example, about the space for the head on the back seats.
As there the complaints end because the combi bodery means that even the great devils will, in this regard, be comfortable.
Let's see done quickly
I'm going to talk about the interior very quickly so I don't rehearse too much.
This is an almost successful design, my only remark about the central tunnel that seems poor.
There, I would have liked a slightly more inventive design, given that the car looks so elegant.
The seats are comfortable and the time when you could complain about seats or too short backages is over.
Lateral guidance has also improved markedly compared to model 206.
As for the space, the increase in the dimensions of the bodywork is also noticeable.
The combi also sees the lack of space above the head already mentioned disappear.
A trunk in the trunk
The most important thing about this vehicle is its luggage compartment.
I have to evaluate this one as very accessible (also thanks to the rear swiveling ice) and a rather easy tie-up.
Blind spaces are equipped with stop elastics which constitute an ideal compromise.
It is not bulky and can be extended while being able to keep fairly heavy objects.
Let's stop the volume.
According to the tables, 428 l in the basic configuration, which is in relation to the competition a rather average figure.
Apart from the Škoda Fabia Combi, the best-selling vehicle of this category in the Czech Republic.
If we compare the 207 SW with the new generation of Mlada Boleslav's product, we see that the Peugeot remains very noticeably behind, the difference being 52 liters.
When it comes to leaving abroad or loading a stroller, this figure is almost critical.
But, if I had to bring out the advantages, I would mention the remaining underbody after the reversal of the rear seats perfectly straight, or a very loot step.
120 horses spread over four cylinders
The car we tested was equipped with a four-cylinder Otto engine with a volume of 1.6 l and a power of 88 kW.
And in fact, that's what a 1.6 should look like.
It is silent, consumes little and, above all, it grows well.
If I compare it with the equivalent produced by Škoda which often gives the impression of having an exhaust pipe blocked by a mop, then I can only be enthusiastic.
Let's go through tariffs
There's not an affordable price for everyone.
However, we must be aware that we tested a fairly well equipped car, with a spacious interior and a very good engine.
The basic price of a vehicle with a 1.4-litre Otto engine amounting to 329 900 Kč is still passable.
The vehicle we tested costs from 410 900 Kč, which is already enough.
The Premium equipment, also tested, increases the price of 80 000 Kč.
However, in addition to airbags, automatic air conditioning, automatic wipers, an automatic control of the rear windows...
In reality, the vehicle ultimately costs 531 900 Kč.
That's a lot, but try to add additional equipment to the Fabia price and you'll get a very similar number.
All you have to do is choose the brand.
The integration of Slovak pupils into British schools is doing poorly
The number of children from Eastern European countries in British schools is increasing, raising concerns about the evolution of local education.
The integration of Eastern Europeans faces a series of obstacles for the moment.
British schools even see cases where conflicts between immigrants and descendants of the original inhabitants turn into violence.
The case of northern Kent is beginning to worsen the conflicts between those remaining and immigrants of Slovak origin is a good illustration of the problem of the integration of children from Eastern Europe.
Arguments, chicane and fights between students have been transposed into the relationships between parents.
The situation went so far that the police arrested in Chatham a Slovak woman who was hitting with an iron bar a ten-year-old student.
The culprit defends himself by claiming that the boy had insulted him with racist remarks.
The police also had to intervene following the attack on a Slovak immigrant carried out by two teenage girls.
The young girls had allegedly made racist remarks to this man and threw stones at him.
"When we were coming home, a young man climbed onto the bus stop and started spitting on us.
When I told him to stop, he responded with apples and pears and then he discovered his buttocks, "described another unpleasant adventure a mother of Slovak students.
There are complaints made by both parties.
One of the restants went so far as to describe the conflicts with the immigrants as a struggle for survival.
The cases mentioned above show that the atmosphere in British schools between the inhabitants of origin and immigrants is beginning to be tense.
70 thousand Slovaks who have come to find work are recorded in Great Britain.
And about 30 thousand Slovak pupils attend British schools.
Cuba is the most beautiful island in the Caribbean
For visitors, this is truly an island of freedom.
Everything you expect from your holidays can come true if you make a good choice.
Golden and white beaches like snow, high waves or a calm sea like a pond.
Palms and all inclusive with waiters offering you on the beach a pizza, ice cream or intoxicating cocktails.
Kitesurfing, golf and roulette.
On the islands of the Caribbean Sea, you are not going to find this list only in its entirety, but enriched.
However, there is only one island on which you will find much more and it is Cuba, the largest and most beautiful island of the Greater West Indies.
In the time of the Spaniards, Cuba had been the bastion of their invasion of America.
Christopher Colomb described it as the most beautiful place the human eye has ever seen.
Havana has become the depot and place of transhipment of the treasures that the Spaniards had stolen and that they were transporting to Europe.
Then came the American Era.
The Hotel Nacional was erected at the very beginning of the 20's.
It was Lucky Luciano, one of the leaders of the U.S. mafia, who built it, since all that was a crime in the United States (especially under prohibition) was admitted and supported in Cuba: drugs, gambling, prostitution.
Among his clients were, among others,
Winston Churchill, Ava Gardner, Frank Sinatra.
In Havana, high-rise buildings grew and cars, belonging to the cult symbols of the 50's of the last century, circulated on the wide boulevards.
Ernest Hemingway bought a property in San Francisco de Paula, near Havana, and in Cojímar he had his yacht.
The stars of show business and politicians from all over America left their signatures on the walls of the Bodeguita del Medio.
What about today then?
You can leave your autograph yourself on the walls of the Bodeguita of Havana.
In the bar of the Hotel Nacional, a luxury hotel, we will mix the cocktail of your choice.
And these cult cars are still circulating in Havana, since jigoulis and once imported fiats have already for a long time, in a climate so salty and moist, rotten.
Although Havana, especially the oldest part, is substantially decrepited, nowhere else in the surrounding area there are as many splendid colonial monuments as there are precisely there.
Other places are becoming more beautiful, such as Trinidad.
Since tourism brings the money if necessary, its development has the green light.
During the last fifteen years, new hotels have grown not only in Havana, but especially in Varader, on the coast of Holguín province, and also on small islands such as Cayo Coco, Cayo Guillermo and others.
Cuba still offers a fantasy that is unique in the world and will be appreciated especially by lovers of small trains.
The cane had re-entered from plantations extended into the sweets on a narrow track by small steam and motor trains.
Their rolling stock has not been renewed for decades and this is how we can see small locomotives, the contemporary of which are only elsewhere in museums.
Where to direct your steps?
The majority of visitors do not miss the most well-known places.
So there is no need to write a lot about Varadero or Havana.
If not to recall that in the property of Hemingway, already mentioned, there is a museum and that one who likes this writer should not miss the visit.
The Viňales Valley in the west of the island is one of Cuba's most picturesque corners.
Exuberant vegetation grows on limestone soil.
Mogotes, limestone balloons and rocks rise in candlelight from the bottom of the valley, and from the fertile earth having caught in their bowels, even its rotten rocks are covered with a very dense vegetable carpet.
The valley is the place where Cuban tobacco is probably cultivated of the best quality.
You will be able to experience the final form of this product if you visit one of Havana's cigar factories.
Someone may also find it interesting that this is where Major Zeman’s Chilean episode was shot.
Trinidad
Ancient city founded shortly after the Spaniards colonized the island.
It is the trade of slaves and that of sugar that have brought him glory and wealth.
The richness was embodied in the beauty and city-window character of this small city.
Koloniální španělská architektura,výrazně ovlivněná pozdějšími francouzskými osadníky, za čtyři staletí téměř nesměnila.
Trinidad, located between the sea and the Escambray mountain range, is such an outdated place that still in the 50' years of the last century, there was no road that would connect this region with the rest of the country.
This isolation allowed him to stand aside.
We weren't building anything, and that's why we didn't demolish anything either, everyone was content to have a roof over his head.
If we have, in Trinidad, more time than an afternoon, then it is worth also going to see interesting places in the area, such as Playa Ancón beach or the Sucreries valley.
Then, in the evening, it is customary to go to the Casa de la Música which comes alive after sunset and where the music does not deafer until early morning.
Baracoa
Some refer to this village located in the extreme east of Cuba as the most beautiful of the island.
This opinion is certainly already influenced by the path that leads to it.
The two roads that lead from Guantánamo must cross high and rugged mountains and cross an almost unmarked landscape of human activity.
UNESCO has inscribed Cuba's eastern pitfall, thanks to its unspoiled landscape, on the World Heritage List.
We make the best chocolate, in the church, there is the cross of Christopher Columbus (in reality, it was born about a hundred years after the journey of Columbus) and from the hill where stands the old castle and the current El Castillo hotel, we see several mountains table, the most famous of which is El Yunque.
Regarding coffee, rum, cigars, the Sierra Maestra mountain range, the Bay of Sows and Isla de Pinos Island, Tropicana cabaret, the shrine of the patron saint of Cuba Caridad del Cobre, the Santeria, African religions practiced by the descendants of former slaves, about all this one could fill a number of pages.
However, as they say precisely, it is better to see once.
In Afghanistan, allies are passive, say Americans
According to the United States, the lack of soldiers and necessary equipment affects the course of the mission in Afghanistan.
Defence Minister Robert Gates said NATO should outline a concrete plan for the years to come.
The mission in Afghanistan does not proceed as it should, agreed in Edinburgh, Scotland, representatives of countries that have troops in the southern part of the country.
In addition to the growing protest by the Taliban movement, the eight states involved are now also discussing future plans and the coordination of allies.
While the United States this weech through Defense Minister Robert Gates calls NATO troops for greater activity, Britain sees as a priority the strengthening of the authority of the Afghan government and the intensification of development aid.
"Evolvement in Afghanistan is perceptible, but military power can only be part of the solution.
The other is to allow residents themselves to start a new development of the economy and security," British Defense Minister Des Browne told the BBC.
Ninety percent
Afghan insurgent activity is, according to U.S. military data, the most intense in the past five years.
The number of violent actions increased by 27 percent compared to last year, up to 60 percent in the southern Helmand province.
NATO countries have about 40 thousand troops in Afghanistan, including nearly a quarter in the southern part.
However, according to the United States, allies have reached their absolute limit and in the organization and equipment of the troops.
Concretely, they ask for more helicopters, soldiers and experts for training Afghan troops.
“We’ll have to seriously reflect on concrete goals for the period ahead, as well as how to achieve them,” Gates said.
NATO Secretary General Jaap de Hoop made similar remarks today.
"I'm not happy with what we have on land and in the air in Afghanistan.
We have about ninety percent of the soldiers and equipment we would need, and that’s not enough,” De Hoop told Reuters at the end of three-day talks with the Japanese government in Tokyo.
Who's passive
In recent months there have also been conflicts among the countries involved in the issue if all the allies are doing everything possible in Afghanistan.
For example, Germany has been criticised for its passivity.
“The Germans have a relatively large representation in Afghanistan.
But they are engaged in areas where violence is minimal, so the fighting demands they are subjects are not as stringent as those in the southern and eastern parts of the country where we operate,” Gates said.
Britain’s tabloid Sun this week called the German soldiers lazy.
"Afghan laziness discovered: the Germans are playing, while ours are fighting," Sun wrote in a document supplemented by photos of German soldiers playing table tennis.
The German newspaper Bild switched to the counter-attack by publishing the photo of a British troupe during a rugby match in the southern part of Afghanistan.
The debt of the state will rise to a trillion in 2009
The burden of state debt exceeding 84,000 kroron rests with each Czech.
The total debt amounted, at the end of September, to 842.7 billion kroron.
The government had planned to borrow 159.2 billion crowns this year.
Thanks to a better-than-expected change in the savings of the state budget, the ministry has reduced the expected amount to 152.8 billion kronor.
The debt of the State of the Czech Republic rose towards the end of September to 842.7 billion kroron.
During the nine months of this year it increased by 40.2 billion crowns.
However, as of June, it decreased by 13.4 billion crowns.
Today, the Ministry of Finance has thus confirmed its data on the debt of the state dating from the beginning of October.
The expense of a debt exceeding 84,000 kroron rests with each Czech.
Throughout last year, the state has fallen into debt to more than 111 billion krorons.
"For the moment, it seems that, thanks to a smaller deficit projected for next year, one could exceed the border by only a trillion crowns in 2009.
Next year, the debt is expected to be between 900 billions and a trillion crowns,” Patria Finance analyst David Marek for the iHNed.cz server said.
Next Finance analyst Vladimír Pikor's forecast is similar: "We could exceed the trillion in 2009.
The precise date will depend on the next budget that we do not yet know.
If it appeared that the situation on the political scene was changing, that politicians were ready to save more, the date could be postponed to 2010.
“I don’t expect that change,” he said.
Debts increase
The debt of the State consists of the debts of the central government and it is generated mainly by the accumulation of deficits of the State budget.
Government debt is financed by treasury bills, annuity securities, direct bonds or, for example, borrowings from the European Investment Bank.
The domestic indebtedness of the state has increased this year by 38.5 billion to 719.4 billion crowns.
The external debt of the state increased this year for the moment from 1.7 billion kroron to 123.3 billion kroron.
The debt of the negotiable-called negotiable state reached at the end of September 803.3 billion kroron and from June it decreased by 13.7 billion kroron.
There was a 6.5-year average state debt requirement.
"Total debt increased interannually in the first half in the third half by 13 percent, which is, given the current good health of the economy, a figure far too high.
It is interesting that the increase is generated mainly by annuities where it reaches 20 percent.
“It’s bad for the debt to grow, but on the other hand it indicates that there will be room to negotiate when the pension reform comes,” Pikora said.
Best than we expected
It follows from the government's financing and debt management strategy for 2007 that the government had planned to borrow 159.2 billion krorons this year.
However, at the beginning of September, thanks to a better-than-expected change in the savings of the State budget, the ministry has reduced the expected amount to 152.8 billion crowns.
The sum consists mainly of the deficit of the state budget, which will clearly reach 76 billion krorons this year, instead of the 91.3 billion crowns initially planned.
Secondly, they are the maximum sources provided for the Czech Consolidation Agency, i.e. 13.3 billion krorons, the reserve of 10 billion for the payment of pensions, the financing of state annuities for 43 billion krorons and the repayments of loans from the European Investment Bank amounting to 1.8 billion kroron.
She now appeared before a court in Khartoum for appointing a teddy bear
Britain’s teacher tried in Sudan for insulting Islam was sentenced Thursday night by Khartoum court to 15 days in prison and deportation, her lawyer said.
The Briton was accused of having left pupils from 6 to 7 years old to give the name of Muhammad to a teddy bear while any representation of the prophet of Islam is illegal.
She was punishable by lashes.
The 54-year-old British teacher at the Unity High School in Khartoum, Sudan, was arrested at her home on Sunday and charged with violating Islam and sedition under Article 125 of the Sudanese Criminal Code, following several complaints from parents of pupils at the Sudanese Ministry of Education.
The story actually goes back to September, when this teacher asks her students, aged 6/7, to choose a name for the teddy bear of the class.
“Eight names come out of the mouths of the children, including Hassan, Abdullah and Mohammed,” says school principal Robert Boulos.
Finally, after a vote in the classroom, 20 out of 23 children chose Mohamed as their preferred name.
Mohamed is, of course, the name of the Muslim prophet, but above all a very common name in Sudan.
The children then made a book for the class with the photo of the bear followed by the caption “My name is Mohamed”.
The bear itself had no labels with this name, but the problem is simply that of the representation of the prophet considered an insult to Islam.
One of Gillian Gibbons' Muslim colleagues, a teacher at the same school in Sudan, said he knew her well and that she would never have done anything that could be insulting to religious faith, "I just regret that she asked the children to vote for a name," he said it was only an "innocent mistake."
Opinion shared by many students of the teacher who describe her as "very caring towards her students" and "who never speaks of religion in the classroom".
Recall that the first name Mohamed is also the most given middle name in Great Britain, it is written in English in 14 different ways.
This name often chosen by Muslim families is a way of honoring the prophet (often given to the first child of a family).
But what are the rules regarding the use of this name?
For example, can you give it to a toy?
Of course, this is a matter of interpretation.
They did not reach an agreement on Wednesday on the future status of the province, during the last session of negotiations in Vienna.
At the end of the day, the failure.
Kosovo Serbs and Albanians completed a sixth and final discussion session in Baden, Austria on Wednesday morning without overcoming their differences about the future status of the separatist province.
"It is regrettable that the parties have not been able to reach a status agreement," European Ombudsman Wolfgang Ischinger said at a press conference in Vienna.
Stressing that peace in the region was “at stake,” his U.S. counterpart, Frank Wisner, urged Belgrade and Pristina to uphold their commitments to preserve peace and dialogue beyond the end of negotiations.
"There is no provision for immediate violence, but we are entering a very difficult time," he added, noting that "obvious tensions exist."
End of mediation on December 10
Troika mediators, which includes the European Union, the United States and Russia, will visit Serbia and Kosovo for the last time on Monday.
The future of the province with 90 percent Albanian speakers could become clearer when Ischinger, Wisner and Russian mediator Alexander Botsane-Khartchenko deliver their report to the UN Security Council by December 10.
Discussions in Baden, near Vienna, were the sixth and final negotiating session since the troika was tasked with further mediation by the UN last August.
Americans and Europeans consider that their mediation will end on December 10.
The Russians, who have already stalled in the Security Council the granting of independence in Kosovo, insist on a continuation of negotiations beyond this deadline.
“Russia was and remains committed to a negotiated solution, a compromise solution,” Botsane-Kharchenko said.
Unilateral Declaration of Independence?
After eight years of Kosovo's UN administration, Westerners believe that independence under EU supervision is the only viable solution.
Pristina is ready to proclaim it unilaterally if the Security Council does not decide in its favour.
Belgrade insists on greater autonomy.
“Unfortunately, no agreement has been reached,” said Fatmir Sejdiu, president of Kosovo’s Autonomous Authority, in the Baden hotel where these “last-chance negotiations” were taking place since Monday.
Hashim Thaci, former commander of the Kosovarian Rebellion and future Prime Minister of the province, expressed his regret.
But he added that Belgrade’s autonomy plan “belongs to a past that led to killings and deportations.”
“Domino effect”
Serbian President Boris Tadic said a compromise was still possible, warning the Albanian majority of Kosovo against the consequences of a unilateral proclamation of the province's independence.
In particular, Belgrade fears a "domino effect" in a region still weakened by the wars of independence of the 1990's.
“For Serbia,” he said, “it doesn’t mean a compromise is impossible.”
On Tuesday, the Serbian delegation insisted that any decision should return exclusively to the Security Council, where its Russian ally had the right of veto.
“The parliament of Kosovo will have the last word”
“Only a solution within the Security Council is acceptable to Serbia,” Serbian Prime Minister Vojislav Kostunica said.
“These negotiations lasted two years.
They must end as they have begun: in the Security Council.”
To the journalists, Fatmir Sedjiu had replied that "the Kosovo Parliament will have the last word on the status", adding that any unilateral declaration of independence on the part of the Albanians would be "in consultation" with the West.
Bush snatches an agreement between Israelis and Palestinians
President George Bush announced at the opening of Tuesday’s international peace conference in Annapolis, Maryland, that the Israelis and Palestinians had finally agreed on a joint statement.
He said Israeli Prime Minister Ehud Olmert and Palestinian President Mahmoud Abbas had agreed to immediately enter into negotiations to find a final settlement of 60-year-old disputes between their two peoples.
In the presence of the two men, Bush promised that he would do anything to help them conclude a "peace treaty" before the end of 2008.
In the meantime, the Palestinians must dismantle “terrorist infrastructure” and Israel must end its settlement activities, Bush said, reminding both sides of their obligations under the “road map” for the peace they accepted in 2003.
The head of the White House stressed that negotiations between Israel and the Palestinian Authority chaired by Abbas would aim "to conclude a peace treaty resolving all outstanding issues, without exception, including central issues."
This name covers the three thorny problems at the heart of litigation between Israelis and Palestinians: the future borders of Palestine, the status of Jerusalem and the fate of Arab refugees expelled from their homes in what is now the State of Israel during the 1948 conflict.
Speaking after U.S. President Abbas insisted that the upcoming negotiations be "global and thorough" and cover all aspects of a settlement, citing "Jerusalem, refugees, borders, settlements, water, security, among others."
In turn, Olmert pledged that the upcoming talks would be "direct and continuous" and make "an effort to close them in the course of 2008."
At the end of 2008, Bush set the deadline for the implementation of its coexisting "vision of two states" of two states.
Saudi Arabia has revealed that it has secured a commitment in this direction from Bush before deciding to participate in the conference.
Arabia, whose participation in Annapolis is a success for Washington, is at the origin of a plan, endorsed by all Arab countries, which offers Israel peace in exchange for its withdrawal from all Arab territories occupied during the 1967 war, including East Jerusalem.
Annapolis marks "a crossroads in the history of the Middle East, especially because it tackles the roots of the conflict and its central aspects," Prince Saoud said in his interview with the Saudi-powered Arabic daily.
For the prosecutor, the cops are not responsible.
What exactly happened on Sunday?
As every time in this type of miscellaneous facts, official versions and rumors are opposed.
What are the circumstances of the accident?
According to the first elements of the investigation of the General Inspectorate of the National Police (IGPN), a police car was circulating Sunday, shortly after 17 hours, rue Louise-Michel, in Villiers-le-Bel.
“She wasn’t in intervention but on patrol, and was driving at 40-50 km/h, without a beacon,” a police source said.
A green motorcycle of the Kawazaki brand, “unapproved, therefore not allowed to drive on public roads” (see below) and driven by two young people without helmets, circulated “at a very high speed”.
“She struck the police car on her left, after a refusal of priority on the right,” a police officer said.
The blood alcohol control on the occupants of the vehicle was negative.
The condition of the car (before high, starred windshield, bumper) testifies to the violence of the shock.
Very quickly, yesterday morning, the prosecutor of the Republic of Pontoise, Marie-Thérère de Givry, announced to have entrusted an investigation for "acts of manslaughter and non-assistance to person in danger" to the IGPN, co-seized with the departmental directorate of public security of Val-d'Oise.
In the afternoon, during a press conference, the prosecutor specifies that the IGPN's investigation, at this stage, dismissed the responsibility of the police.
According to the magistrate, three witnesses of the accident, heard Sunday evening, confirmed "the version of the polices, namely that this mini-bike arrived relatively quickly on their left".
Yesterday, a kind of groove, probably caused by the friction of the feet holds on the ground, showed that the two vehicles remained entangled while the car of the police managed to brake.
The vehicles have been seized and will be subject to technical expertise.
The bodies of the two victims were autopised yesterday.
What happened right after?
Yesterday, a rumor quickly circulated in Villiers-le-Bel, according to which the policies quickly left the scene, thus not lending assistance to the two young people.
The IGPN, while remaining cautious, would also rule out “any serious misconduct” regarding this point.
"This is a more difficult aspect of the investigation, which requires more investigation, on which you have to be very careful," a police source said.
Libération met with an eyewitness from those moments following the accident.
One of his windows overlooking precisely the stage.
“We immediately came down, with my cousin who is a nurser in the hospital, to try to revive them,” says the witness.
There was nothing to do.”
He then saw “a completely hagging policeman, who was limping.
Two others were trying to resuscitate one of the young people, the fourth was talking on the phone.”
Faced with the tension that quickly surrounded the scene, and, it seems, to the certainty that those present of the unexpected situation of the young people, the policemen were taken in the car by colleagues who arrived at the scene.
According to this witness, the rescue arrived "about twenty minutes after the departure of the police".
They also performed cardiac massages in vain.
"I will not let it be said that the police services did not provide assistance to young people.
These kids were rescued.
Firefighters arrived right away.
Everything has been done in an attempt to save them,” the prosecutor said.
Tension is rising in Pakistan
Pakistani police on Monday cracked down the first demonstrations since General Musharraf established a state of emergency two days earlier.
In the city of Lahore, in the east of the country, about 2,000 lawyers protesting the measures taken under the state of emergency were wounded by tear gazes used by the police, according to witnesses.
The latter responded by throwing stones, injuring police officers.
At least 350 lawyers were arrested.
Scenarios similar to Karachi and Rawalpindi, or police assigned and injured lawyers.
Many would have been questioned.
In Islamabad, lawyers at the Supreme Court’s bar called for a general strike and announced demonstrations, following a wave of some 500 arrests over the weekend of opponents, human rights activists and lawyers.
Streets giving access to the Supreme Court were stranded Monday morning to prevent the rally.
Other demonstrations reportedly took place in Multan (centre) and Peshawar (north-west).
On Monday, the lawyers’ movement garnered the support of religious parties grouped in the powerful Muttahida Majlis-e-Amal alliance whose president “urged the population to send flowers to the judges who voted against the state of emergency and rubbish to those sworn before Musharraf.”
“Musharraf’s Promise Doesn’t Keep
Pakistan’s Supreme Court is directly targeted by the exceptional measure proclaimed on Saturday night.
In the next few days, she had to decide on the legality of the re-election to the presidential election, on October 6, by indirect suffrage, of President Musharraf.
The President of the Court, Iftikhar Mohammed Chaudhry, has been ousted and replaced.
“Everything we attend is illegal, unconstitutional and contrary to Supreme Court rulings,” the magistrate told The News newspaper.
Musharraf’s promise to leave the head of the army and become a civilian president “don’t hold anymore” after the establishment of a state of emergency, Deputy Information Minister Tariq Azeem said Monday.
That he abandon his military uniform was expected by November 15, the date of the end of his first presidential term.
The Deputy Minister of Information also confirmed that the January elections could be postponed.
Moreover, the Pakistani government has denied persistent rumours in the country that President Musharraf has been placed under house arrest by his deputy chief of the armies.
More than one-third of pregnancies remain unforeseen
This calculation takes into account unwanted pregnancies (24%) as well as ill-planned or unforeseen births.
Even today, more than one in three pregnancies (36%) is not planned, reveals a study conducted by the National Institute of Demographic Studies (INED), forty years after the vote of the Neuwirth law that liberalized contraception in France.
This calculation takes into account unwanted pregnancies (24%) as well as ill-planned or unforeseen births.
The different methods of contraception such as the pill or IUD still have a failure rate of 5% to 6%, estimates INED.
The liberalization of contraception has nevertheless allowed a better "mastery of fertility", according to the institute which notes that the rate of use of the pill among women aged 20 to 44 has increased from 5% in 1970 to 60% today.
Eight out of ten births would be well planned today.
Even calculated to the nearest month for one in five couples and if possible in the spring, season judged as the most pleasant to have a child.
Spectacular repair on the space station
It took more than seven hours of work in space to astronaut Scott Parazynski and his crewmates of the International Space Station (ISS) to carry out the spectacular repair of a torn solar panel, essential for the continuation of the station's scientific activities.
A risky outing that has accumulated records because of its duration, its distance from the habitable modules, the speed with which it was imagined, the tools “tinkered” by the astronauts to carry out the repair.
The problem arose Tuesday as the astronauts unloaded the Harmony module, a large cylindrical part that soon welcomed the European and Japanese scientific laboratories (see box).
This module is a kind of landing dock for laboratory modules.
You have to be able to supply them with electricity.
The second task of the crew was therefore to move an electricity production module by solar panels weighing 17.5 tonnes, already present on the ISS, in order to set it to its final position.
After moving it, the crew began the redeployment of the solar panels of the module that have a wingspan of 76 meters.
And that's where one of the panels, unfolding like accordions, was damaged on nearly a meter by a cable that got stuck.
The deployment has been halted so as not to further damage the panel.
The astronauts, who were originally supposed to perform a control exit from the Discovery Shuttle, and then go to repair another solar panel whose rotational system was defective, were forced to devote themselves to the damaged panel.
And it was Scott Parazynski who was chosen to go caracolate at the end of the 30-meter length of the remote-controlled arm of the shuttle added to that of the station to carry out the repair.
It is one of NASA's best "spacewalker".
Large, resistant, very skillful, it has very developed torso and long arms.
At the age of 46, this training doctor was tasked to "operate" the "injured" solar panel.
After precisely inspecting the damage, he severed the faulty cable and installed kinds of "splints" on the damaged area.
He was helped by a second "spacewalker" left near the airlock and, from the inside, by other astronauts including Peggy Whitson, the commander of the crew.
The tool he used, an insulated mini-hockay cane to avoid electrocution on solar panels producing several hundred volts, was designed and "tinkered" by the astronauts aboard the station.
Once the operation was completed, Scott Parazynski waited until the panel was fully deployed before making an inventory of his tools and regaining the inside of the station.
Yesterday afternoon, the astronauts took advantage of a half-day of relaxation before today, seven astronauts did not return to the Shuttle Discovery for a return to Earth scheduled for Wednesday.
EADS stock sanctioned on the stock exchange
EADS shares are declining sharply currently on the Paris Stock Exchange, after the aeronautics and defense group announced that it would have to spend between 1.2 and 1.4 billion euros to cope with the delays of the A400M.
EADS loses 4% to 21.96 euros currently on the Paris Stock Exchange.
The group was forced to review its operating income forecast for 2007 as a result of the delays caused by the slow progression of the A400M's engine development, which determines the aircraft's inaugural flight.
The cost to mitigate the delay in the delivery of its military transport aircraft, announced in October, is "between 1.2 and 1.4 billion euros including more than 1 billion for Airbus", announced the parent company of the European manufacturer EADS.
Because of these expenses, EADS will be forced to announce new operating income (EBIT) targets for 2007 when presenting its quarterly results next Thursday, it adds without further quantified details.
The group also indicates that estimating the new charges is consistent with the six-month delay.
As a reminder, the operating result of EADS fell by 86% in 2006, mainly because of expenses related to the delays of another program, that of the very large carrier A380.
Initially, The group planned a first delivery of the A400M to the French army in October 2009.
The choice of status quo
There will be no suspense, Sunday, at the exit of the polls: the Russians will opt massively for the party of President Putin, United Russia.
Confirming their aspiration for stability, even authoritarianism, after a very locked campaign.
Three days before the parliamentary elections, Russian President Vladimir Putin today sends to voters a televised message on public channels, already registered but whose content is kept secret.
He does so as the leading list of united Russia, the pro-Kremlin party whose victory promises to be overwhelming.
Yesterday, the president did not leave anything about it by receiving the foreign ambassadors, simply delivering a new charge against the West accused of interference - its favorite theme during the campaign.
"We know the price of a real democracy and want honest, most transparent and most open elections, elections without snags," he added.
In the eyes of the opposition, this is far from it.
She denounces a campaign marred by pressure.
Communist leader Gennady Zyuganov says there was "never such dirty elections, even in Yeltsin's time".
After last weekend's crackdowfle in the protests, former chess world champion Garry Kasparov, sentenced to five days in prison for illegal demonstrations, remains denied a visit, according to his lawyer.
“The Russians have kept the mentality of homo sovieticus.”
Behind these unsuspected legislative elections loom two much more open questions:
- Who will succeed Putin in the presidency?
The official newspaper published yesterday the date of the first round of the presidential election, March 2, 2008; the candidates have until December 23 to make themselves known.
Elected in 2000 and re-elected in 2004, Vladimir Putin cannot seek a third consecutive term.
However, no successor emerges.
- What role will Putin play after March?
prime minister?
Leader of the parliamentary majority and the all-powerful United Russia party that would choose the government and the president?
In any case, in the legislative and in the presidential elections, the outgoing power will triumph.
It's a tradition.
"The Russians have kept the mentality of homo sovieticus, they do not feel masters of their destiny," says sociologist Lev Goudkov, director of the independent center Levada.
The historian Nikolai Kopossov, of the State University of St. Petersburg, goes back further: civil society has fallen behind in this Christianized country five centuries after Europe; the famous community spirit has delayed the formation of individualism.
“Putin reconnected with the model of a paternalistic state, perfectly accepted by the population, especially since this new paternalism was not followed by terror, but by a certain economic ease,” says Maria Lipman of the Carnegie Foundation.
Today the Russians "renounce willingly the personal responsibility" they had briefly shown after the break-up of the USSR.
“What’s the point of thinking?”
The phenomenon affects all social strata, including the business world.
And the administrative elite intends to preserve the status quo: 65 governors (out of 85 heads of Russian regions) lead United Russia’s local lists.
New freedoms imported from the West are often synonymous with chaos, as in the 90’s.
The opinion prefers stability.
On behalf of which the Russians will also not vote for extremists.
Conclusion of Tamara Cherednichenko, 54-year-old teacher: “What’s the point of thinking?
“Those in power aren’t too bad, why change them?”
A heavy memory
After more than 60 years of confidentiality, Bad Arolsen’s Nazi archives, which trace the fates of 17.5 million victims of the Hitlerian regime, are freely accessible.
The 47 million archival documents, stored on 27 km of linear in Bad Arolsen (Hesse), were so far consulted only for "humanitarian" purposes, i.e. in an individual and nominative manner, at the request of a former victim or his beneficiaries.
The eleven states in charge of their management - including Germany, France, Israel and the United States - agreed in May 2006 to open them to researchers and historians.
The process of ratification of this agreement by all States has been completed, and openness has been effective since yesterday.
Sensitive information
Historians' access to Bad Arolsen will make it possible to carry out research "in particular on the displacement of prisoners, the population of the camps and the state of health of forced workers", explains Reto Meistern, the director of these archives managed by the International Committee of the Red Cross (ICRC).
Until recently, several States, including Germany, were opposed to the opening to the public of these nominative documents, because of the sensitivity of certain information.
Such as the supposed homosexuality or mental disability of some victims of deportation.
The registers of concentration camps or arrest warrants established by Gestapo had been gathered after war for a practical purpose: to find civilians deported or subjected to compulsory work and, possibly, to provide them with proof of their internment, in order to pave the way for their compensation.
Even today in Bad Arolsen, more than 300 permanent employees process tens of thousands of individual requests.
However, for part of the scientific community, access to Bad Arolsen is of limited interest.
“There’s nothing fundamentally new to waiting for these documents,” Professor Wolfgang Benz, director of the Centre for Research on Anti-Semitism at the Technische Universität in Berlin, said in 2006.
The EU and India want to reach a free trade agreement in 2008
Currently, Indo-European bilateral trade already reaches nearly 60 billion euros per year.
The EU is India's largest trading partner and accounts for 18% of its foreign trade.
The European Union and India hope to sign a free trade agreement in 2008, said European Trade Commissioner Peter Mandelson and his Indian counterpart, Kamal Nath.
EU foreign ministers last April gave the green light to the European Commission to start negotiations to sign Free Trade Agreements (FTAs) with India, South Korea and the Association of Southeast Asian Nations (ASEAN). Indo-European bilateral trade already reaches nearly 60 billion euros per year.
The EU is India's largest trading partner and accounts for 18% of its foreign trade.
LUE is also its first foreign investor, but India is only the 9th trading partner of the EU, according to figures from the European Commission.
"A free trade pact will boost both economies enormously" and "India would improve its access to a market of 450 million prosperous Europeans," Mandelson said.
Europe represents the first or the second market for each of the first ten products exported by India, said the European Commissioner. The Asian and European giants exchange annually for "47 billion euros of goods" and for "ten billion euros of services", said this week Danièle Smadja, head of the delegation of the European Commission in New Delhi, regretting that bilateral trade has "not yet reached its potential".
(Source AFP)
The Bank of England takes note of the concerns by offering 10 billion pounds over five weeks
The bank of England said on Thursday it was anxious to lighten the current return of concerns about credit conditions, and announced an offer of ten billion pounds at the base rate of 5.75% over five weeks, an offer of an unusual duration.
“To alleviate concerns that financial market conditions will be particularly tight at the end of the year, and to give banks greater certainty in how they organize their liquidity positions over this period, the Bank intends to offer a significant proportion of its projected supply of reserves during the maintenance period commencing on December 6 in the form of a five-week open market operation,” it said in a statement.
The bank specifies that 10 billion pounds (14 billion euros) will thus be placed on the market on December 6 at 12:15 GMT, at the base rate and until January 10.
This is the first time that the BoE has placed five-week liquidity on the market in an open market operation.
These are normally done within a week.
BoE said in a statement that it is "ready to take further steps to keep interbank longing rates" day-to-day online with its base rate.
The day-to-day interbank rate was 5.829% on Wednesday.
The three-month rate stood at 6.6%, the highest since September 18.
Since the beginning of the financial crisis of the summer, the sums placed on the market by the Bank of England were accompanied by a high penalty rate that had discouraged banks from resorting.
According to some rumors, corroborated by the evolution of the price of the pound against the euro, many had preferred to subscribe to the sums put on the market by the European Central Bank, at more advantageous rates and with a more assured discretion.
UMP and NC refuse to consider PS proposals on purchasing power
The UMP and New Centre groups on Thursday refused to discuss the articles of the proposed socialist law on purchasing power, which amounts to a rejection of the text.
Inscribed in a socialist "niche" (session on the initiative of a parliamentary group), the text declined a dozen measures adopted Tuesday by the national office of the PS including the 50% increase of the premium for employment, the restoration of the floating TIPP, a check-transport or the regulation of rents.
UMP and NC having voted against the examination of the articles (180 votes against 115), the session was adjourned at the end of the general discussion which gave rise to exchanges, sometimes lively, between the majority and opposition a few hours from Nicolas Sarkozy's televised intervention on purchasing power.
The leader of the PS deputies Jean-Marc Ayrault has announced that his group will represent all of its proposals in the form of amendments to the amending finance bill considered by the Assembly next week.
A new festival is born
Following numerous rumors about the creation, by C3 Presents, of a new music festival in Philadelphia, the promoter/producer announces the Vineland Music Festival in New Jersey, in partnership with Festival Republic of British producer Melvin Benn.
“For our company, it’s an honour to work with someone who has inspired the current festival movement in America,” Charlie Jones of C3 told Billboard.com.
C3 produces the Lollapalooza Festival in Chicago and the Austin City Limits Music Festival.
Vineland, New Jersey, is a summer camping destination.
The festival is scheduled to take place from August 8 to 10 on a 500-acre private farm about 40 minutes from Philadelphia.
Formerly known as Mean Fiddler, Festival Republic Director Melvin Benn is one of the world’s most respected festival producers.
In 1989, he took the helm of the Reading Festival in the United Kingdom, which attracts some 80 000 people annually.
In 1999, Melvin Benn added the Leeds Festival to his portfolio and, in 2006, Festival Republic created Henham Park’s Latitude Festival in Suffolk.
Since 2002, as co-owner, Melvin Benn has also been responsible for the production, licensing and organizational tasks of the Glastonbury Festival, which can now accommodate up to 177 500 people.
Calling Glastonbury “the most inspiring event” he’s ever attended, C3’s Charlie Jones says his and Melvin Benn’s companies are working in parallel to give the region a European-style festival-event.
“We chose Philadelphia as our market and worked diligently with the Fairmount Parks Commission to create a festival in downtown Philadelphia,” Jones said.
“We were in talks with the city and the Commission was motivated and excited by this project.
“Unfortunately, we’ve got bogged downed into politicians because of the current administration.
“Fortunately, we’ve been able to chat with Melvin Benn and we’re about to create a great festival on an exceptional site that will ultimately serve the people of Philadelphia.”
C3 Presents resurrected the Lollapalooza Festival in 2005 at Grant Park in Chicago, having stood out in the festival landscape in 2002 with the Austin City Limits Music Festival.
Both events recorded gross revenues of $9.8M and $11.3M respectively in 2007.
Both festivals are held in an urban setting.
“Melvin Benn’s European model is a country festival, while ours take place instead in urban green spaces,” Jones says.
The objective is to merge, in one way or another, the two formulas to give both an impression of a country festival to the European and urban American.
Vineland is about halfway between Philadelphia and Atlantic City.
“The Vineland community, including the mayor, enthusiastically supports the holding of this event,” says Charlie Jones.
The latter refuses to reveal the terms of the agreement, but affirms "that they are interesting enough to allow to invest in such an event and to host a festival that will hopefully have a long life."
Charlie Jones says the hosting capacity of this festival is "very large", like that of 80 000 people at the Bonnaroo Music Festival in Tennessee.
He says that invitations have been issued to the groups, but that nothing could yet be confirmed when going to press.
“Vineland will be rock-flavored, but the music will be varied, hoping to attract all sorts of viewers,” Jones said.
His C3 partners, who received the Top Independent Promoter Award from the latest Billboard Touring Awards, are Charlie Walker and Charles Attal.
Montreal faces the Terminator
It's not easy to attract Hollywood movie sets in Montreal when none other than Terminator opposes it...
This seduction mission is one of the delegated functions.
"Politically difficult" mandate because California Governor Arnold Schwarzenegger denounces "runaway productions".
Is it difficult to play in the legs of the “Governator”?
“You have to be careful, it’s the industry that decides where it’s going.
If she finds that the conditions in Montreal are favourable, she will go.
Our role is to offer those they will judge the best,” he said.
The Race for Festivals
For the moment, however, Denis Turcotte's priority is the promotion of local cinema.
The race for the Oscars has begun.
He will be from all festivals on the West Side, whether Sundance, Denver, Seattle or San Francisco, to present Quebec films, highlight them and ensure that filmmakers make interviews.
The Age of Darkness had a beautiful showcase at the 30th Mill Valley Film Festival a few weeks ago.
It will premiere at the Palm Springs International Festival in January.
Shake Hands with the Devil premiered in Santa Monica and premiered at the 30th Starz Denver Film Festival in November.
Quebec also presented four feature and four short films at the American Film Institute Fest this month.
Will there be an end-of-year rally in the stock market? Experts divided by the sub-prime crisis.
Less than five weeks from the end of the year, investors are already rubbing their hands hoping for the arrival of the traditional year-end rally.
However, this year experts aren’t as sure as it’s going to happen.
Banif believes that "from a statistical point of view, the month of December on the stock exchange usually has positive behavior.
However, it is not appropriate to make forecasts based exclusively on statistics, since given the current context, the uncertainties prevail in the markets, at least in the short term ".
Although they are not in favour of the stock market gaining momentum during the last weeks of the year, these experts note that "the stock market feeds through the existence of liquidity, ready to invest given the lack of alternatives with guarantees, especially fixed income, affected by the effect of leakage to quality values both in long periods and in short."
For this, they believe that the stock market will have a rather lateral behavior, not free of volatility "especially because we do not know the impact of the likely fall in Fed rates, given the high level of crude and the danger of stimulating inflationary pressures"
Javier Barrio, BPI's sales manager in Spain, agrees that this is not the right time to say there will be a rally.
"It's not the best thing," the expert said.
Ibex, Spain's stock index, has lost nearly 4% since Nov. 8 when the index closed at 15,945.7 points.
However, not all the experts have such a negative vision.
Intermoney analyst Juan Solana believes that Ibex 35 could close the year at 16,000 points thanks to the reorganization of portfolios and traditional contributions to pension plans that occur every year during these dates.
However, the expert nuances that things will be a little different this year since he believes that the rally will take place from the second week of December, after the bridge of the Constitutional Day (December 6).
The analyst does not consider that the volatility will affect the market trend.
Federico Olucha, an analyst at Inversis Banco, estimates that we are close to technical levels and "this is why we could observe a rebound of the index that could be caused depending on the information coming from the European Union regarding the consequences of the crisis on the credit market".
The analyst hopes these will be positive.
Analysts agree to choose the values that will be responsible for leading the Ibex to new maximum odds.
Solana, from Intermoney, claims that "this year the great values are back for him".
The expert would include in the portfolio the two major banks and a few manufacturers "because when the date approaches, the electricity sector will be very expensive".
While, Federico Olucha, of Inversis Banco assures that the increases will be due to banking and the industrial sector.
Builders will also be able to take advantage of this rally, in the event that they get involved.
"ACS for several months has been recovering positions and we hope that the other builders like Ferrovial and FCC will follow the same path," explains the expert.
Cyclical consumption will be in the final part of the year due to increased sales in the Christmas sales season.
On the other hand, the expert believes that technology companies will also do it very well, although in this case there is not much representation on the Spanish market.
Five times for seven years
Over the past seven years, only for two occasions in December has been a bearish month.
The authentic year-end rally took place in 2003, during which the stock markets emerged from the crisis caused by piercing the technological bubble.
This year, when Ibex 35 recovered 28.17%, the month of December recorded an increase of 6.68%.
It will be necessary to see if 2007 is the fifth consecutive year of winnings (for the moment the Ibex has increased by 8.36% since January) and if it succeeds computer on its year-end rally.
The Banque Populaire will open 200 offices open 12 hours from Monday to Saturday
The Banque Populaire has decided to renovate a large part of its offices.
A total of 200 are the banks located in Spain's most commercial areas.
These branches, which will operate under the Popular Max brand, represent a big change for the bank.
Also for the rest of the Spanish organizations, since it is the first group that has decided to start betting on the uninterrupted opening of its agencies until 20h30, and to open Saturday from 10h to 20h30.
Another group that has also reiterated several times that it would like to amplify the schedules of its branches, BBVA, even if it has not yet decided to take the first step.
It is about to reach an agreement with the unions to close 75% of its agencies on Saturday instead of opening an afternoon, but not to the public.
The results of the experience of the People's Bank will be decisive so that other organizations may or may not adhere to this initiative, which coincides with the schedules of shops.
It is precisely this goal that the Banque Populaire is seeking.
Attracting the autonomous customers circulating in these areas to make their purchases in SMEs and street shops chosen to open.
The bank wants to open these 200 branches throughout Spain in about 18 months, since this is not the opening of new agencies but a renovation of those already existing.
To do this, the organization will modernize the branches that it already has in commercial areas, adapting them to the profile of customers of the different streets.
In this way, the amplification of schedules is accompanied by a different design from the interior of the branch and a new design, more current, with brighter colors.
Bank sales manager Ángel Rivera says this renovation doesn't involve large investments, but the hiring of staff, since the number of employees will increase from six to eight or nine per agency.
The agencies, which will also have space for SMEs to meet there, will sell non-financial products.
Positive Experience for the Group
The Banque Populaire has already tested its initiative in three agencies in Madrid.
And the experience has been positive, as Ángel Rivero explains.
The branches of Murillo Brave, O'Donnell streets and the Gran Vía of Madrid are the streets to have been chosen, and successfully apparently, according to Rivero.
Banque Populaire currently has 2,500 branches.
And 60 others that operate under the Mundocredit brand, specialized in the case of immigrants, also with very wide schedules, which even open on Sundays and public holidays.
In these PopularMax agencies they won’t copy the BBVA model, where many of its agencies have a wide range of non-financial products for its sale.
“We don’t want to compete with our customers,” Rivero notes.
For the moment, they have reached an agreement with Telefónica to sell mobile phones, with staff outside the bank.
Telecinco doubles for the first time the stock market value of rival Antena 3
We've got there.
With this phrase Paolo Vasile, a delegated adviser to Telecinco, expressed yesterday his satisfaction, at the closing of the stock market, when he found that the channel he runs doubled the value of his rival, Antena 3.
A single aspect tarnished his joy: "what hurts me is not the fact that we have increased more but that we have lowered less," he said.
However, however, he emphasised the fact that in a weak market, ‘we have fallen less’.
Telecinco finished the day with an increase of 2.54% yesterday.
This gain stabilizes its loss to 15.66% over the past year.
The public value of the company controlled by Mediaset (with 52% of the capital) and announced by Vocento (13% more) thus reaches 4,488.88 million euros, according to data from Bloomberg.
His rival Antena 3, which yielded 1.52% yesterday and accumulates a decrease of 40.5% since January, costs half, 2,193.46 million.
The value of the other publicly traded communicating companies amounts to 3,571 million in the case of Sogecable; 2,518.53 million in that of Prisa (the publisher of Cinco Días) and 1,779 million in that of Vocento.
According to Vasile, the comparison with Antenne 3 is due to the fact that we are talking about two similar companies.
The relative fact represents what we are able to do, in the same market, at what price and how we make it profitable in terms of audience.
Telecinco announced last week that it plans to become the first TV channel this year to exceed 1,000 million gross advertising revenues, as Giuseppe Tringali, the managing advisor of Telecinco and Publiespaña, the subsidiary that manages the group’s advertising, said.
In order for this announced data to be real, the television channel would have to record an increase of 3.6% in its invoicing for advertising compared to 965.4 million in fiscal year 2006.
For its part, the net invoicing of Antenne 3 increased by 1.6% in the first nine months of the year (up to reaching 734.4 million) while net television revenues increased by 0.7% (630.4 million).
One of the factors that analysts point out for the best relative evolution of Telecinco on the stock exchange is the important pay out it has maintained so far: in 2006, the company chaired by Alejandro Echevarríía distributed 100% of the profit between its shareholders.
Vasile assures that, although it is early to make a decision, this ratio could vary after the purchase of 33% of Endemol and in association with Mediaset.
“We have the official compromise to give a minimum of 50 per cent, although we have always said much more.
This year, I hope that we will be able to make our shareholders happy, to those to whom we have already given securities with the 33 per cent Endemol.
According to analysts, at the moment the market is showing signs of fatigue.
Lehman Brothers recently reduced earnings estimates on Telecinco in 2008 to 4% and in 2009 to 7%.
This is due, they explain, to the decline in projected revenue growth from 10.5% to 8.4% in 2008 and from 5.5% to 5.1% in 2009.
The same company lowered Antenne's earnings forecast 3 to 4.5% in 2008 and 7.5% in 2009.
3 opinions
1.
Ibersecurities recommends buying both stocks based primarily on its significant dividend profitability and long-term sustainable potential.
2.
Caja Madrid sees Telecinco (accumulating) better than Antenna 3 (maintaining) for the 'multiple attractions' and the rise in business.
3.
JPMorgan: it recommends to examine both cases since it had 'similar threats' (a saturated market and a poor economic climate).
The Congress approved the transposition of the Mifid, which came into force on 1 November
In parallel to its parliamentary formality, which ended today with the Congressional vote amendments incorporated into the bill in the Senate, the Government has submitted to a public hearing the regulations that will develop the new law, with the objective of its entry into force before the year ends.
The representatives of the various groups agreed to highlight the effort made by Members of Parliament and Senators to negotiate and make the best regulations to ensure the protection of investors and to regulate in detail the activities of the agencies so that the markets function effectively.
Mifid, which amends the Securities Market Law, involves the modernization of financial markets, at a time when it strengthens the protection of the investor, improves the powers of the leaders of the National Securities Market Commission (CNMV) and promotes cooperation between the various leaders of the European Union.
The new regulations will make it possible to lend financial consulting services to both specialized social reasons and to natural or legal persons and creates a new type of financial services (ESIS), financial consulting companies (AFIs), which merge with securities companies, securities agencies and portfolio management companies.
In addition, it increases the number of systems for the execution of transactions on financial instruments, so that it is possible to add multilateral trading systems and order internationalization systems to regulated secondary markets, which compete with current stock exchange managers.
The Act also requires investment service companies to disclose on the market information on key aspects of its business profile, risk exposure and forms of risk management, and requires them to keep a record of all transactions they carry out, in order to facilitate control by CNMV.
By going through the Congressional Economics Commission, several amendments have been added, including one that highlights that tenured debts will be considered a "complex" financial instrument given its high risk to the investor, which has been demonstrated with what happened with the debt of high-risk U.S. mortgages (subprime).
In addition, they took advantage of the transposition of management took the opportunity to legally delineate the functions that graduates in Economics may have 30 years after in 1977 was approved, the Royal Decree which delineates the professional functions reserved for economists.
For its part, the Senate has incorporated the creation of new figures in the financial sector, such as that of the mediator, who will work on behalf of a company, who will not require the authorization of the CNMV and who will be able to lend its services of marketing products and attract new clients to different investment firms at the same time.
The harmonised consumer price index rises by five tenths in November, up to 4.1%
This indicator, which is then used by Eurostat to incorporate it into the calculation of the rate of inflation in the European Union, provides a ballance on price developments in Spain during the month of November.
Its publication responds to the policy of Eurostat and the European Central Bank (ECB) by offering data comparable over time and in quality to those produced in the United States.
The advanced indicator is calculated using the same process used for the Harmonized Consumption Pricing Index, but using various statistical modelling methods to estimate the information that is not yet available for publication.
INE recalled that the information provided by the leading indicator is only indicative, because it does not necessarily have to coincide with the definitive data that will be revealed on December 14.
"CPI will continue at relatively high levels"
Second Vice-President and Economy Minister Pedro Solbes said the 4.1% increase in the CPI in November is a "time figure", but at the same time he predicted that the price index will continue on "relatively high" levels in the coming months.
In any case Solbes said in the corridors of Congress that "although the figure is not good" Spain's inflation differential about monetary union continues to be "more or less" the same as in recent years.
He also explained that in November "there was less surprise" than during the previous month, when the Government was not facing such a high increase.
"We hoped for a figure around 4%," acknowledged the Minister of the Economy compared to the data announced today.
Virging plans to recover with Northern Rock 42,000 million euros over three years
Northern Rock’s deposits fell to more than 50% to 12,000 million pounds (16,800 million euros) since it came into crisis around the middle of September and had to resort to an emerging credit from the Bank of England.
At that time he amassed a few record deposits above 25,000 million pounds, a figure that is gradually dropped in two and a half months because of the mistrust of its customers and despite the 100% guarantee of this money that the Government has offered and will maintain until the end of the crisis.
Virgin, which would rename the organization with its financial trademark Virgin Money, needs to seize around a quarter of the revenues of British banks that will be deposited in the next three years to obtain these remaining 18,000 million pounds until reaching the target of 30,000 million.
The group of tycoons Richard Branson, known for its creard advertising campaigns in the United Kingdom, intends to spend 50 million pounds (about 70 million euros) per year on advertising and marketing to achieve its goal.
Northern Rock this week has named the offer of the Virgin Association, in which three other companies participate, including his favorite to save him from bankruptcy.
The mayor of Totana has been arrested for an alleged plot of urban corruption
The Civilian Guard arrested today in the early morning the current mayor of the Murcian commune of Totana (of the People's Party) because of its alleged relationship with the plot of urban corruption discovered this week.
ADE plus, one of the secretaries of the municipal council and the chief of police of the municipality have also been arrested.
José Martínez Andreo has replaced last May me Juan Morales, current right-wing deputy, and hitherto municipal councillor of the town hall, and who according to the sources of the investigation consulted by the SER Chain, could be the 'leader' of this plot.
Officers continue to excavate the municipal premises and those of the Urban Planning Council and the possibility of new arrests is not ruled out in the coming hours.
In addition, the lawyer of Juan Morales, the main suspect in the plot of urban corruption, discovered earlier this week, has been imputed.
As the SER Chain indicated yesterday to the lawyer of the deputy 'popular party' Juan Morales, he was arrested by leaving Morales' home with important documentation in his possession relating to the plot.
Moreover, according to the sources of the investigation, the purpose of the investigation is the presumed collection of Morales' commissions in exchange to facilitate the signing of an urban agreement with a Galicia-building company to reclassify 200 hectares of land.
For the time being, there are eight people detained.
Bono agrees to lead Spain's Socialist Party candidacy for Toledo and presides over Congress if they win elections
Former Defense Minister José Bono has accepted the offer of the President of the Government and the Secretary-General of the Socialists, José Luis Rodríguez Zapatero, to be at the head of the list of the Spanish Socialist Party for Toledo for the next general elections and to be president of the Congress in the event that the Socialists win the general elections.
Thus the organizing secretary of the Spanish Socialist Party, José Blanco, and Bono himself announced it during a press conference after the meeting that took place this afternoon at the federal headquarters of this party with Zapatero.
The head of the Executive justified the offer made to the former minister because "it is important to count on the best" in political life and Bono "is among the best".
Moreover, he stressed that "yes it seems" that the politician of La Manche will be the candidate of the socialist group that will preside over the Congress if the socialists will win the next elections.
Bono would replace Manuel Marín as President of the Congress, who made public on November 15 his decision not to stand at the next general election and abandon his political career to devote himself to the fight against climate change in academia.
The ex-minister has acknowledged that the President of the Government has not stopped insisting that he return to the political vanguard since he abandoned it two years ago.
Moreover, he pointed out that, even if the citizens already know who will be the economic vice-president if the Spanish socialist party wins the elections, his party wanted to announce the one who will preside over the Congress, in an "act of transparency".
If he reaches the job, Bono hopes to turn the House into "a house of respect and not insult or cry" and make "it more and more similar to the citizens".
"Sometimes it seems miserably that the only premises in Madrid where you can't speak quietly and calmly is Congress, the President of the Government in the Senate on certain occasions has been interrupted 26 times."
In the same way, he had words of praise for his current president, Manuel Marín and "his know-how" and he did not want to pretend that he was already occupying his position so as not to fall, as he remarked, in what his opponents could consider "domination".
Climate propaganda
Given that the movement against climate change submists persecution without mercy both the skeptics of its predictions and those who give priority to other political and social battles, it must demonstrate iron coherence.
This is all the more the case for a leader of the movement who is president of the Government like Zapatero and who believes that this fight is more important than that of Islamist terrorism and who even intends to sign a "new contract for the planet".
This approach obliges him to explain why the action, or inaction, of his Government contributed decisively so that Spain is at the head of the European Union in the non-execution of the Kyoto Protocols.
Who are those responsible for non-executivity, in which sectors it occurred and why his Government, that of the contract with the planet, did not avoid it.
Moreover, he must clearly explain to the Spaniards what measures he will take to curb climate change.
What companies will be affected, what habits of citizens will have to be changed, what individual and collective energy savings we will be forced to do, what economic consequences it will cause.
That is to say, who will sacrifice and who will pay to save the planet.
But there has been and will be no explanation.
Precisely because it's about sacrificing and paying.
Measures against climate change, real measures, are unpopular.
Expensive, uncomfortable and threatening to the accounts of companies and individuals.
Up to one hundredth of the essence suggested by the Spanish Socialist Party seemed lectorally so dangerous to Zapatero that he rushed to deny him.
That is, it is about saving the planet with nothing, only with propaganda, with empty slogans of any real consequences.
With sentences that have impact, commissions, committees, protocols, new positions.
With these contracts with the planet, this gentleman so useful for election campaigns that does not speak, that does not denounce and that does not require, beautifies meetings and inspires tenderness.
Provided that this is only limited to being a purely virtual contracting party and which does not claim that we travel by bicycle or we refresh ourselves with the spectrum.
The mayor and the head of the local Totana police arrested for an alleged plot of urban corruption
The Spanish gendarmerie has arrested the mayor of the Murcian town of Totana, the "popular" José Martínez Andreo, the head of the local police, the secretary of the City Hall and a suspicious hotel contractor for possible urban crimes, have now informed sources of the investigation.
The councillor was arrested at his home and was taken to the town hall, where at the moment many agents gathered, who also presented themselves to the Function of City Councillor of Urban Planning and to the municipal enterprise for the management of the Industrial Soil and Housing.
These three judgments are in addition to the six judgments made last Monday in the provinces of Galicia, Murcia and Madrid, in an operation relating to the requalification of more than 2 million hectares of agricultural soil to urbanize them so that the Galician company Nuaria can build 4,000 housing units, after the payment of illegal commissions during the last legislature.
Moreover, two other persons have not been arrested but they are imputed in the judicial inquiry, which the No. 1 Court of Totana hears.
The first six inmates have now switched to a judicial provision.
According to the sources, Totana's previous municipal councillor, who is currently an autonomous parliamentarian of the PP party, Juan Morales, is being investigated.
In addition, the ex-wife, owner of a real estate agency currently registered in Totana, has been imputed, as well as the current fiancée of the former municipal councillor, who resides in Murcia.
The director and owner of the Nuaria Group, the lawyer and entrepreneur of Vigo (Galice) Manuel N.A., were arrested in Nigrán (Pontevedra), as well as Pablo José M.G., director of Suelo de Inmonuar, agency of the Nuaria Group, through which the bribes would have been made.
The investigation is the responsibility of the Group of Urban Offences of the Central Operative Unit (UCO) of the gendarmerie whose agents, in addition to the arrests, carried out eleven inspections, the majority in companies related to detainees and located in Madrid, Vigo, Murcia, Pontevedra, Las Rozas (Madrid) and Totana.
Only one person has therefore been arrested in Totana, in short, the owner of a well-knowned poultry company in the region, which may have played the role of intermediary.
The Nuaria Group was responsible for the development of the largest residential complex of the Murcian commune of Totana, which would involve the construction of more than 5,000 dwellings, a golf course and two hotels with "spa".
The company has acquired 2.2 million square meters of land in Totana that have been reclassified and its project would involve doubling the population of the municipality, which currently has 25,000 inhabitants.
The Nuaria Group consists of companies such as Autesa and Inomonuar, which take care of real estate development; Conycase, which manages Vigo's car parks in Coruña, Venezuela and Fernando el Católico Square; Hogartel, which deals with direct marketing; Preconiza, which focuses on the promotion, sale and installation of building elements.
