A colleague passes the information on the introduction in the Criminal Code of crimes on downloads on the Internet:
A. The downloading of a song would be an offence punishable from six months to one year.
On the other hand, the theft in a CD store for a value of less than 400 euros is considered only as a fault (Article 623.1).
B. The theft in a store for a value of up to 1,000 euros is already considered an offence, but the penalty is less than that imposed for the download (Article 234 of the Penal Code).
C. If you steal a car and make it 40 hours later, the penalty is less than that imposed for the download (an article 244.1).
D. It is less serious to participate in a fight than to participate in compact disc traffic.
Participating in a tumultuous fight involves a sentence of three months to one year (Article 154 of the Penal Code) and the trafficking of CDs would involve a sentence of six months to two years
(art. 270 of the Penal Code).
E. Sexual harassment in the workplace is considered less serious than downloading a film, according to article 184.2 of the Criminal Code.
F. The distribution of films protected by copyright and without the authorization of authors is more punishable than the distribution of pornographic material to minors (Article 186).
Finally, if my colleague is in the real then someone exaggerates.
